{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition","id":1386135,"title":"Ten tips for running the Second Inquisition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-06T12:02:14-07:00","id":1386135,"title":"Ten tips for running the Second Inquisition","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2020/05/ten-tips-for-second-inquisition-in.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2020/05/ten-tips-for-second-inquisition-in.html\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2020/05/ten-tips-for-second-inquisition-in.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2020/05/ten-tips-for-second-inquisition-in.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Why all the secrecy? Why not just go public, let people protect themselves?&quot;</i><br /> <i>&quot;Listen. Every week there's a panic about some puny little bug. Now how do you think it would be if this got out? Hm? You'll have paranoia, you'll have vigilantes, you'll have people running back to religion in droves. The next thing you know, you'll have the Archbishop up for Prime Minister. I don't fancy living in Iran, do you?&quot;</i><br /> -Mike and Vaughn, <i>Ultraviolet</i><br /> <br /> The Second Inquisition is a development for the Fifth Edition of Vampire: The Masquerade. It is an alliance of hunter groups that has arisen in the past decade and inflicted hundreds, if not thousands, of casualties on the vampire race. They have also pulled off seemingly impossible victories like the destruction of the Tremere Council of Seven, destroying all the Kindred of London, and playing an instrumental role in the collapse of the Giovanni leadership.<br /> <br /> The organization has also caused massive upheavals in the Kindred world. The Camarilla has started using Cold War spy techniques and almost Game of Thrones communication techniques (&quot;Send the ravens!&quot;) to avoid being tracked by the seemingly omnipresent foe that can hack phones as well as monitor every call. Their government ties and access to War on Terror authority as well as military-grade weaponry means that many undead believe that they could destroy the vampire race. But how dangerous are they and what way should they be used? Here's some suggestions from me on this.<br /> <br /> <b>1. The Masquerade still exists and isn't going away</b><br /> <br /> One misconception is that the Second Inquisition has blown the Masquerade completely and the world's governments are now hunting vampires globally. This is not the case at all. The Second Inquisition is a group of individuals, secret societies, and cabals within public organizations loosely allied together to kill as many vampires as possible. They are all collectively of the mind that the Masquerade is better for everyone, though, because of the societal upheaval that revealing vampires exist could cause. Their motivations may vary but the majority of them believe firmly that this is a terrible idea and will actively cover up the existence of the undead like the monsters they hunt. The Second Inquisition DOES have more than enough evidence to expose vampires if they wanted to, though, and that makes outright destroying them harder than it might seem.<br /> <br /> <b>2. The Second Inquisition is not new</b><br /> <br /> There is no actual Second Inquisition any more than there is a <i>Project: Twilight</i>. The Second Inquisition is a nickname for the sudden upswing in successful vampire hunts conducted by mostly pre-existing organizations that have been menacing Kindred for centuries as is. The Society of Leopold isn't the Second Inquisition, it is the first Inquisition. It has just reunited itself with the Vatican under the WOD version of Pope Francis and received funding from sponsors in the European Union as well as United States. It's joined by the Knights of Saint George, FBI Special Affairs Division (SAD), Arcanum, Bob Schnoblin's Goblins, and a dozen other groups. Once they started sharing information and working together, the number of vampires they began to kill skyrocketed. Even so, they're about as united as the Nine Traditions, which is to say not at all.<br /> <br /> <b>3. The Second Inquisition benefits from vampire in-fighting</b><br /> <br /> The cleansing of London turns out to have been orchestrated by the 4th generation methuselah Mithras as a way to purge his political enemies. Both the destruction of the Vienna chantry and Mausoleum are all but stated to have been done with the help of &quot;inside men&quot; with the latter being arranged by the Hecata. The entire reason the SI exists is because the Camarilla attempted to use the US government's security apparatus against the Sabbat and Anarchs before blaming the latter in a classic projection defense. Many vampires, when confronted with the SI, will attempt to use it against their enemies rather than form a united front. As Pam from True Blood answered a hunter psychologist's, question, &quot;How much loyalty do you feel toward your race?&quot; &quot;None.&quot; This doesn't mean the Second Inquisition isn't dangerous by itself, it just means that the Kindred's many defeats are being their own worst enemy.<br /> <br /> <b>4. The Second Inquisition is knowledgeable</b><br /> <br /> Previously, Kindred had the advantage that most hunters had about as much knowledge about vampires as any student of pop culture. The Imbued in Hunter: The Reckoning were encouraged to be written as ignorant as possible in order to maintain dramatic tension. The Second Inquisition are not remotely ignorant. Indeed, for all intents and purposes, one should consider its members to own a copy of Vampire: The Masquerade's main book. Clans, ghouls, sects, bloodlines, Disciplines, and so on. The thing is, for the most part, the Second Inquisition doesn't care about these things. They are interested only in how to destroy the undead and answering existential questions that the Kindred themselves have no answer for (like, &quot;how do the dead move?&quot;). They don't necessarily understand what they know but they've captured many vampires who have squealed like pigs all their secrets. This helps SI leaders do unconventional things like framing vampires for murder, plotting to set them against one another, and other non-traditional hunter plots.<br /> <br /> <b>5. The Second Inquisition is subtle and patient</b><br /> <br /> Contrary to the assumption that many Kindred have, the majority of SI agents will not immediately react to the discovery of a vampire's haven by sending in SWAT teams to gun them down or dropping a hellfire missile down on an identified Elysium. First of all, the SI must preserve its own secrecy and is not interested in a few stragglers. The SI may actually monitor vampires for months or even years before striking as they are attempting to get a full sense of the massive world they have found out about. Some SI agents may want to slaughter all of them whenever and wherever they find them but these are the minority. They are also the ones most likely to get a SI cell or base slaughtered in the aftermath.'<br /> <br /> <b>6. The Second Inquisition is rich, not omnipotent</b><br /> <br /> The Second Inquisition has more resources than the original Inquisition and technology the vast majority of elders do not understand. However, it is not actually a single group but a large number of pre-existing groups with friends in the world's varying governments. Even then, they cannot lend aid to one another easily. Let's face it, it's hard to explain why a FBI agent might be sending a bunch of rocket launchers to a orthodox Catholic group in Italy even if they could acquire them in the first place. Also, they've used a lot of their discretionary income to update existing hunter groups but even its leaders' deep pockets can't spend indefinitely to fight a menace that its governments don't even believe exist.<br /> <br /> <b>7. The Second Inquisition is mortal, not supernatural</b><br /> <br /> The Second Inquisition can have support from other supernatural groups in your Chronicle. Certainly, the Technocratic Union would probably have agents peppered through it. So would other groups. The SAD had a Kinfolk, NWO Agent, and Pentex operative in its regional directors. Indeed, the Camarilla almost certainly has agents in the Second Inquisition despite its many precautions by members used to said beings. However, it should fundamentally be a grass roots mortal response to Kindred arrogance. Despite this, there's no reason why &quot;unusual&quot; devices and anti-vampire weapons can't be justified by individuals who wouldn't mind pruning the population of the undead (even among the undead). It also does have access to Numina via hedge mages, faithful mortals, psychics, and other low-level human powers. Enough that Dominate 3 isn't enough to solve all the undead's problems.<br /> <br /> <b>8. The Second Inquisition isn't listening to your phone (probably)</b><br /> <br /> The Second Inquisition isn't using PRISM to monitor the entire internet for any mention of Camarilla, Anarchs, Brujah, or Beckett. Even if they could, they wouldn't be able to sort through all of the data or justify it to other government branches. The Kindred don't understand their enemy or its capabilities, so that's partially why the SI continues to bedevil them. They can hack the computers and phones of those Kindred they identify but it's usually a much more personal as well as slow-going process. The paranoia about one vampire potentially exposing many others is not entirely unjustified, though. How screwed are you if they have a bug in Elysium? The Succubus Club? Or more? Perhaps very or perhaps not at all as everyone uses an alias. It's all up to the Storyteller. It's also possible that the guy monitoring those places will stick his findings in a pile of papers that will never be read or be an agent of another power.<br /> <br /> <b>9. The Second Inquisition fights smarter, not harder</b><br /> <br /> It is possible for the Second Inquisition to send a Navy SEAL team to your haven to gun you down or call a drone strike down on your location. This is the dumbest most panicked response that they can imagine. The Second Inquisition knows that not only are they hiding their activities from vampires but they are hiding from the parts of the government that may not react well to their activities. That doesn't mean that such panicked ill-conceived attacks don't happen, but they will be the outlier unless the undead have backed the group into a corner or gotten the drop on them. At the very least, expect attacks to happen during the day and escape routes to have been blocked. They may also work to make it appear as if it was another vampire's minions or regular law enforcement. They are the underdogs in this fight and can't afford to lose as many members as taking down a typical coterie in hand-to-hand takes.<br /> <br /> <b>10. The Second Inquisition can and will be beaten</b><br /> <br /> Ignoring the game is called <i>Vampire: The Masquerade </i>and not <i>Hunter: The Sterilization</i>, the Second Inquisition is not actually an existential threat to all of vampiredom. It might be a threat to one of the sects or many cities but it doesn't have the oomph to win overall. The moment they chose not to destroy the Masquerade was the moment they lost the war. <i>Humanity</i> can defeat the Cainite race, not any small group of it no matter how well equipped. SI agents are subtle, patient, rich, and knowledgeable but so are many vampires. The Camarilla has enough resources to attack the agencies behind the SI, let alone its operatives in it. The Anarchs are capable of repopulating as well as falling back into regular humanity. Even the Sabbat, diminished as it is, is an army larger than the SI as well as a supernatural one. The trick is that any individual vampire can be killed by them and most vampires are more terrified of that being them than any overall threat to their race.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-06-2020, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T13:02:24-07:00","id":1386153,"title":"","content":"A first-rate summary and very useful.<br /> <br /> I quoted a character in one of my games a few years ago on another thread, making a similar point to the Ultraviolet quote at greater length...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">&quot;Vampires are dead. There is </span></span><i>no </i><span style=\"color:#696969\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">electrical activity in their brains. None. Yet they think, they feel, they reason, even though science tells us that all of these things are impossible without brain function. Their mental processes cannot be physical. They must be spiritual. Don't you see the implications of that? </span></span><i>Vampires are empirical proof that souls exist</i><span style=\"color:#696969\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">&quot;Our society is essentially secular. Few would say this so bluntly, but our ability to coexist with others of different faiths relies, deep down, on the unstated assumption that religion is merely harmless nonsense. Or, as Professor Dawkins argued after 9/11, exceptionally dangerous nonsense. But nonsense nonetheless. Our entire humanist moral consensus rests on that foundation. We can say unequivocally that the tortures of the Spanish Inquisition were wrong, because we don't for a moment believe that those tortures saved their victims from a far worse pain that would last for an eternity. Thanks to the scientific method, the only suffering we consider is that which we can see, observe, prove to be real. Reinstate unequivocal belief in the soul, and that will change with terrifying speed&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">&quot;Prove to the world at large that the supernatural exists, that science doesn't have all the answers, and it won't only be the jihadis who'll be empowered. Unlike Monty Python, I </span></span><i>would </i><span style=\"color:#696969\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">expect the Spanish Inquisition, and new Crusades, and new witch crazes. Society as we know it would struggle to survive, and even if it did, the victims would number in their millions, almost all of them innocent&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">&quot;So no, I don't intend to destroy the Masquerade. The consequences would be too horrifying to contemplate&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> The only victory that the Second Inquisition can win is a pyrrhic one, but they can still keep the vampire population in check. I'd add point 11 - The Second Inquisition is morally ambiguous. It's not impossible, as we saw in the Fall of London, for the new, secular breed to agree a precarious truce with vampires. Some are as careless of human life as vampires or their medieval predecessors. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T13:14:22-07:00","id":1386161,"title":"","content":"I remember those quotes and I have to say, &quot;That person is a Technocrat and completely clueless to how non-materialists think.&quot;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Still, a good one. It certainly is a perspective that you don't want to expose the supernatural to the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-06-2020, 08:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T23:48:34-07:00","id":1386286,"title":"","content":"11. <b>The Second Inquisition are not the good guys</b><br /> <br /> One could make a compelling argument that the destruction of all vampires is a good thing. Even the best of the Kindred race will probably a few innocents before their Final Death. The Hunger and Beast are inescapable (unless you're a Thin Blood--and even then it's a crapshot). However, the Second Inquisition is full of fanatics that feel that they are justified in doing whatever their quest requires. Zeal and righteous anger do not lead anywhere good in the World of Darkness, though. Inquisitors will kidnap, torture, and execute anyone they feel is an ally of the undead. This includes vessels, blood bound slaves, and innocent pawns. Unlike vampires, the Second Inquisition cannot mind-wipe people to cover up their existence and so are much more likely to kill in order to hide their organization's secrecy. Hideous medical experiments, terrifying black sites, and other moral compromises are things the SI are involved in. Vampires are monsters by nature but may do less damage than the SI cell that fakes a terrorist attack in order to give it operational freedom in the region. Ditto the ICE operative who decides to sell detainees to vampires because he realizes how much money can be made in the Blood Trade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T02:10:12-07:00","id":1386331,"title":"","content":"The SI still remains entirely unbelievable. Hold on, let me write something out:<br /> <br /> 1. The Masquerade still exists because it makes for a better story.<br /> <br /> 2. The second inquisition is entirely new.<br /> The factions that compose the SI would have never worked together in any other edition. Hunters were meant to be clear underdogs, not &quot;The man&quot;. <br /> <br /> 3. The second inquisition should infight a lot. But they don't, because plot.<br /> Religious terrorists, big government, and cryptic scholars? not a great recipe. <br /> <br /> 4 the second inquisition has somehow managed to sort out mountains of false information and agree on things.<br /> But they still use UV lights because they liked <i>Blade</i> a lot.<br /> <br /> 5. The second inquisition is brazen and short sighted.<br /> Why would you even hunt vampires? The smart ones doing this with zeal are rare, The zealous stupid ones are plentiful and won't amount to much, and the worldly ones would see there's more benefit to working for vampires rather than against them.<br /> <br /> 6. The second inquisition is logistically infeasible.<br /> They can't have so much resources at their disposal without exposing themselves to vampires.<br /> <br /> 7. The second inquisition is supernatural<br /> Because how can you apply so much plot armour onto mere mortals? How can you explain the obvious logistical problems without magic?<br /> <br /> 8. The second inquisition can't really sneak up on anyone with auspex.<br /> How do you bug a house or museum when the vampire's auspex ratings are 3+? Electronics make noise dude.<br /> <br /> 9. Vampires would fight both smarter and harder than the inquisition.<br /> They've had centuries of practice and time to get entrenched with local authority and build up vast information networks.<br /> <br /> 10. The second inquisition should never have hit the ground running. They should've been beaten before day one.<br /> But the Camarilla got hit with the idiot stick and Dominate got hit with a nerf bat.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you wanna run them, run them. Just remember: Critical thinking is the enemy, just have a blast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 05-07-2020, 05:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T02:42:32-07:00","id":1386335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1386331#post1386331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The SI still remains entirely unbelievable. Hold on, let me write something out:</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1. The Masquerade still exists because it makes for a better story. </div> </div> </div>Yes, that would be normally the motivation. Most people don't want to write crappy stories.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. The second inquisition is entirely new.<br /> The factions that compose the SI would have never worked together in any other edition. </div> </div> </div>And the fact they are now is why they're doing so much better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. The second inquisition should infight a lot. But they don't, because plot.<br /> Religious terrorists, big goverment, and cryptic scholars? not a great recipe. </div> </div> </div>Hence why I recommend they be disunited and have infighting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4 the second inquisition has somehow managed to sort out mountains of false information and agree on things.<br /> But they still use UV lights because they liked <i>Blade</i> a lot. </div> </div> </div>Because not even vampires know everything 100%.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5. The second inquisition is brazen and short sighted.<br /> Why would you even hunt vampires? The smart ones doing this with zeal are rare, The zealous stupid ones are plentiful and won't amount to much, and the worldly ones would see there's more benefit to working for vampires rather than against them. </div> </div> </div>Because they're a bunch of religious zealots, government spooks, and people who have seen how dangerous vampires are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6. The second inquisition is logistically infeasible.<br /> They can't have so much resources at their disposal without exposing themselves to vampires. </div> </div> </div>Yes, hence why the vampires know they exist versus not knowing they exist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 7. The second inquisition is supernatural<br /> Because how can you apply so much plot armour onto mere mortals? How can you explain the obvious logistical problems without magic? </div> </div> </div>Really?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 8. The second inquisition can't really sneak up on anyone with auspex.<br /> How do you bug a house or museum when the vampire's auspex ratings are 3+? Electronics make noise dude. </div> </div> </div>A vampire that has auspex on at all times is a cripple from all the feedback that a 5 year old could stake. Auspex is for when you concentrate on something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 9. Vampires would fight both smarter and harder than the inquisition.<br /> They've had centuries of practice and time to get entrenched with local authority and build up vast information networks. </div> </div> </div>That's in the article.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 10. The second inquisition should never have hit the ground running. They should've been beaten before day one.<br /> But the Camarilla got hit with the idiot stick and Dominate got hit with a nerf bat. </div> </div> </div>With all due respect, you seem to have a lot of invincible Tremere and Camarilla depictions. What exactly are their weaknesses?<br /> <br /> If you wanna run them, run them. Just remember: Critical thinking is the enemy, just have a blast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-07-2020, 05:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T05:42:35-07:00","id":1386369,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"> logistics</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#70757A\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">/l\u0259\u02c8d\u0292\u026ast\u026aks/</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>noun</i><br /> [COLOR=#878787 !important] </span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">1. the detailed organization and implementation of a complex operation.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">2. the activity of organizing the movement, equipment, and accommodation of troops.</span></span></span></span></li> <li>[/COLOR]</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">People love alternate histories, and a prominent alternate history that comes up repeatedly is one where the Nazis win WWII. It's a<b> sensationalist</b> story, not a reasonable one How do they win WW2? Any explanation either involves an inconceivable amount of hindsight, completely ignoring logistical problems the Nazis had, or changing the Nazis in a way that they are no longer Nazis (or changing their enemies in a way that makes them no longer who they were). The Nazis lacked information, materials, manpower... The Nazis couldn't build nukes because they scraped the project as an unrealistic fantasy with the progress being made, and many working on that project were jewish. The Nazis couldn't<i> not</i> go to war with the soviet union, because they were ideological enemies and taking that land was the whole point of the war. They couldn't have just built more wonder weapons because those things needed materials that were in shorter and shorter supply, and the Italians just couldn't have been a worthy ally because... that's a long discussion. The Nazis totally lucked out in conquering France; it was their big achievement and the french just made the wrong moves at the wrong time. In more &quot;realistic&quot; alternate histories, the Nazis fare far worse in conquest than they'd do in reality, not better.<br /> <br /> Vampires aren't the French (There are French vampires, sure, that's not what I'm talking about). They're not making moves like the french. They can't put all their eggs in one basket because they're not as united as the french. But in a lot of ways, the SI are worse than the Nazis when it comes to alt history.<br /> <br /> <br /> 1. The SI would have a terrible time procuring materials. Incendiary ammunition isn't easy to come by or order, chaoscopes or whatever are expensive. The more things they have, the more visible it is to vampires and the easier it would be for vampires to shut them down.<br /> <br /> 2. The SI would have a terrible time procuring quality manpower. Where do you get people who are good at things that are trustworthy and reliable and would want to hunt vampires? People that definatly aren't plants and are definetly not looking to join the vampires, people who don't have connections which can easily be exploited by the vampires? If you start digging into someone's background, how are you sure someone didn't take notice? Most military types are well documented. Even if you do find great people, how are you sure they're not victims of vampire brainwashing? Even after a mission, how are you sure that nobody's got a directive implanted into them to go postal?<br /> <br /> 3. The SI alliance is no good. Germany and Italy didn't like eachother, they disagreed on a few issues, but they weren't enemies. As much as we like to point at the CIA arming &quot;freedom fighters&quot; that become tomorrows terrorists, What member of the government, who's fighting vampires for truth, justice and the american way, wants to delegate their job to a bunch of religious extremists? What SoL man wants to work with the goverment which has traditionally been their enemy as a tool of vampires? Who wants to work with the satanic arcanum? Why does the arcanum want to work with anybody else?<br /> <br /> 4. The SI alliance can't reasonably contact one another. And if they could, that just heightens the damage a vampire infiltrator can do.<br /> The alphabet hunters are small units hiding within their larger organization. Let's not think about the great strain it would take to hide in this scenario, let's consider how this group would find other groups before their parent organization? How does a hunter group in the FBI contact a hunter group within the CIA? How do they even become aware of it's existence? How does the FBI group get in contact with the Society of Leopold without the rest of the FBI becoming aware of the Society of leopold?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The SI works because it's sensationalist fun. It's pulp fiction. It's not something you should look at seriously, or with any sense of &quot;this is the right way to do it&quot; because there is no right way to do it. We can argue about the thematics of the SI, but logistically and sociologically, it doesn't work and there's not really all that much debate to be had. You might as well try to tell tales of a Nazi alt history that isn't convoluted in the slightest. Because allthough you could come up with a story that makes the Nazis win, they'd need to just make all the right decisions ever, which would hardly be believable. The SI, as written, should logically last between a -getting stomped before they actually start their war- and two years. The only problem the vampires would have is trying to justify the small but not insignificant number of government agents disappearing or going postal. </span></span></li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T07:35:18-07:00","id":1386393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition#post1386135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>9. The Second Inquisition fights smarter, not harder</b><br /> <br /> It is possible for the Second Inquisition to send a Navy SEAL team to your haven to gun you down or call a drone strike down on your location. This is the dumbest most panicked response that they can imagine. The Second Inquisition knows that not only are they hiding their activities from vampires but they are hiding from the parts of the government that may not react well to their activities. That doesn't mean that such panicked ill-conceived attacks don't happen, but they will be the outlier unless the undead have backed the group into a corner or gotten the drop on them. At the very least, expect attacks to happen during the day and escape routes to have been blocked. They may also work to make it appear as if it was another vampire's minions or regular law enforcement. They are the underdogs in this fight and can't afford to lose as many members as taking down a typical coterie in hand-to-hand takes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> list and discussion. This point is also important, and on a related note an area where <i>Fall of London </i>dropped the ball in terms of game design.<br /> <br /> Real tactics and strategy are not what is used in movies, television shows and video games. Real tactics and strategy about getting the best results, and are not about style over substance. The &quot;Blade&quot; rip off bullshit from <i>Fall of London</i>, and similar ways of handling the SI is all wrong. The SI should never, ever just try to go toe-to-toe with any vampires. They should cut off resources, escape routes, opportunities, and move in for the kill - all during the daylight.<br /> <br /> Ideally, the SI should serve a similar role in V5 as did the Sabbat in V1 - a menace lurking at the edges of vampire society. A reminder that Camarilla vampires are not the sole predators and masters of the night. The fire, as compared to the frying pan that is normal vampire society (i.e. &quot;out of the frying pan, into the fire&quot;). The dog the steps of every smug and incautious vampire, and they cannot be defeated with some video game style grand standing bullshit... which is why some gamers hate them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T08:39:13-07:00","id":1386413,"title":"","content":"I'd call this list &quot;how the SI should have been portrayed and used, to make sense in the context of the earlier editions' setting&quot;. But it wasn't. It was presented in a totally makes-no-sense, overpowered and unbelievable manner.<br /> <br /> Really it's the case, IMO, with most of the V5 plot stuff. It's not that they're bad, most of them could be good. It's that they went so overboard with them and it profoundly changed the setting, many times in a way that's basically retconning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 05-08-2020, 05:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T09:56:06-07:00","id":1386422,"title":"","content":"Just because i didn't adress it before: auspex really isn't that much of a hastle to use, and if you rule it as a hasle, would it really be so difficult to use in what should be a quiet museum that's about to host an elysium? Whatabout just before you enter or exit your haven? I find it incredibly balsy that you'd handwave auspex away like that, even if it's a whole lot weaker in V5. Sure, it's inconveneint if every SI agent watching a vampire with auspex gets caught, but isn't that what'd happen? If to make something happen, you have to pretend that rules don't exist, should that thing really happen? <br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> Smart hunters are, probably, the worst enemy of a player who hasn't prepared for them. They're also a little... unfun? You go to rest for the day, you don't wake up, the other players find out your haven burnt down. You either need to catch a hunter whilst they're preparing, arange a trap, or just have a strong haven. I'd grade havens like this: <br /> <br /> Idiot fledgling: <br /> You sleep on a bed in a home unprotected. Nevermind the hunters, if someone opens the curtains you're screwed. I've had a GM assume I've did this once, but fortunately I wasn't in the process of being hunted at the time. You generally shouldn't assume players are doing this. <br /> <br /> Virgin neonate (on a budget): <br /> You travel through some maze-like structures and sleep somewhere hidden. You sleep in a closet, under a bed, in a freezer. You may or may not survive yokel hunters. <br /> <br /> Chad neonate (on a budget) <br /> The above, but you've got a ghoul or two (animal or human) keeping watch, maybe you also sleep within good walls and a strong door. You sleep somewhere people won't look. You would probably survive a yokel, you might struggle with a few. Small chance to make it out of a police raid. Leopold would have to plan this one out; They can get to you, but can they get to you fast enough to avoid the police? <br /> <br /> Ancillae (or a neonate that looks after themselves) <br /> Fenced off area, Strong structure with steel doors, hired security with at<i> least</i> one ghouled and ready to go waco on police, dogs and/or technology, a hidden resting point, a backdoor if shit hits the fan. A chance to fend off a police raid, leopold would most likely lose. <br /> <br /> Elder<br /> Fenced off area, strong structure with maze like features probably built to accomadate the vampire (none of the builders remember the layout) , hired security, dogs, secret passage out. <i>Maybe</i> you could survive a werewolf pack, Mortal hunters would need a lot of firepower.<br /> <br /> Chantry<br /> The Elder, but with wards and more security (because this is a shared haven). <br /> <br /> Vienna prime: <br /> Combine D-Day with <i>Serious Sam;</i> That's what you'd need. <br /> <br /> Nosferatu<br /> First, the hunter must pass through a horde of rats, then flesh eating rats, then they must travel through colourless, odourless poison gas over a surface of high voltage wires. If they cannot climb across <i>the bar</i> and lift the Ton obstacles from the path, they must swim through acid. Should they open the vault, which contains the same hazards as before, they must then<i> find</i> the Nosferatu, who sleeps unseen, among a vast catacomb containing a number of mines and a HIT MARK V toting a balefire thrower and Medium machinegun. Nevermind hunters; you've been preparing for the Niktuku. <br /> <br /> <br /> I also feel that, generally<b>, if you're a neonate and you're allocated a space in someone's territory, that person doesn't want any harm to happen to you as it'd be a big loss of face</b>. They're not going to give you a security detail, but if their information network picks someone up, and they don't secretly want you dead, they're going to either deal with the problem, inform you of the problem and expect you to deal with it, or wait for the right moment and pounce for the sake of prestation. It's great to be an upstanding member or the community, or to have a neonate owe you big; letting the neonate die in your backyard is the worst option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T11:43:53-07:00","id":1386442,"title":"","content":"I generally do the \u201cparanoid clanless neonate\u201d level of security; never sleep in the same place twice, change hunting grounds every few days and regularly top yourself off with quick non-lethal feedings to avoid hunger frenzies that leave attention-drawing bodies.<br /> <br /> Someone in a nightclub who\u2019s left a little lightheaded after some super pleasurable heavy petting with a neck nuzzle (bite, suck a point, lick closed... 6-12 seconds tops) isn\u2019t going to put you on anyone\u2019s radar... particularly if it\u2019s a different person at a different club each time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T12:46:19-07:00","id":1386461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1386369#post1386369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The SI works because it's sensationalist fun. It's pulp fiction. It's not something you should look at seriously, or with any sense of &quot;this is the right way to do it&quot; because there is no right way to do it. We can argue about the thematics of the SI, but logistically and sociologically, it doesn't work and there's not really all that much debate to be had. You might as well try to tell tales of a Nazi alt history that isn't convoluted in the slightest. Because allthough you could come up with a story that makes the Nazis win, they'd need to just make all the right decisions ever, which would hardly be believable. The SI, as written, should logically last between a -getting stomped before they actually start their war- and two years. The only problem the vampires would have is trying to justify the small but not insignificant number of government agents disappearing or going postal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ignoring the whole Nazi comparison...<br /> <br /> I feel like you're attempting to engage not with the Second Inquisition as presented in this thread or the presentation but with your own conception of it. I'll stick with this part because it gets to the root of the matter. You repeatedly have a big issue with the question of, &quot;Where does the Second Inquisition get its soldiers who want to hunt vampires?&quot; This is seemingly one of your big issues with the SI.<br /> <br /> The answer is that there are already hundreds, if not thousands of vampire hunters active in V20. There's the Society of Leopold, The Judges, The Knights of Saint George, the Arcanum, the Muslim organization I forget the name of, an entire branch of the FBI, and a group of NSA that was assembled by one of their generals and then managed to prove that &quot;aliens&quot; exist with science. You don't need more than a few dozen government agents with the already pre-existing vampire hunter groups to suddenly have a lot more power and danger.<br /> <br /> The majority of the boots on the ground are already there because your insistence on other threads, &quot;organized hunter groups do not exist&quot; is not true in Classic V:TM. They're more organized and allied together into one loose alliance but they're not <i>invented</i> for the game. Which is something you've accused V5 of doing. All of your claims, &quot;The Camarilla should be able to smash them&quot; apply to these previous organizations. Except they didn't. You can argue this is stupid and you don't let it happen in your games. That's entirely valid and I'd argue it's weird the Camarilla hasn't smashed the Arcanum as early as 1st Edition.<br /> <br /> However, it's canon and a part of the setting in Classic V:TM. It's not V5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because i didn't adress it before: auspex really isn't that much of a hastle to use, and if you rule it as a hasle, would it really be so difficult to use in what should be a quiet museum that's about to host an elysium? Whatabout just before you enter or exit your haven? I find it incredibly balsy that you'd handwave auspex away like that, even if it's a whole lot weaker in V5. Sure, it's inconveneint if every SI agent watching a vampire with auspex gets caught, but isn't that what'd happen? If to make something happen, you have to pretend that rules don't exist, should that thing really happen?</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit that I would never allow Auspex to detect a recording device as a Storyteller. Heighened senses allows you to hear things you wouldn't normally hear. So, if a SI agent was talking on a phone nearby you could hear them. If you saw a SI agent's aura, though, you would maybe be able to tell that he was hostile or paranoid but not that he's an agent. You could read an object he'd held or touched and maybe get a vision he's dangerous but you'd have to do that first. If you found an agent and read his mind, you could perhaps gain an insight but that assumes that you have spotted one of their agents directly watching you and have that skill. Certainly, Auspex doesn't work like an &quot;I win&quot; button because Kindred have ghouls and agents watching each other all the time. That's part of the Jyhad.<br /> <br /> Also, no Kindred would use Auspex constantly like playing Batman: Arkham Asylum in Detective mode.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1386413#post1386413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd call this list &quot;how the SI should have been portrayed and used, to make sense in the context of the earlier editions' setting&quot;. But it weren't. It was presented in a totally makes-no-sense, overpowered and unbelievable manner.<br /> Really it's the case, IMO, with most of the V5 plot stuff. It's not that they're bad, most of them could be good. It's that they went so overboard with them and it profoundly changed the setting, many times in a way that's basically retconning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everyone is entitled to their opinion regarding V5 and everyone can be have a preferred edition. I do think that the original presentation of things like the Second Inquisition, Beckoning, and so on were severely flawed. I think that they've gradually backepedaled on a lot of things with Chicago by Night's depiction of the SI and Beckoning much more moderate. This is my interpretation of how they should be played and its more based on the latter than the former.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-07-2020, 04:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T13:40:07-07:00","id":1386472,"title":"","content":"Electronics hum. Not sure if premonition would pick up on it, but heightened senses would. Most elysiums are quiet, controlled places where you'd notice that kinda addition. It'd also make it near joke-easy to find an SI agent tailing a vampire to find out where the vampire goes. <br /> <br /> It's not that I don't think organized hunter groups should exist, I just know that the scale of the SI is ridiculous. Vampire hunter organizations need to keep themselves secret from other organizations. Because not only are they ideologically different, they're often ideologically incompatible, and on a purely practical level: If you're well connected and one group is compromised, you're all comprimised. <br /> <br /> In VTM, a single malk with intent could use the wonderful three disciplines to utterly devastate a cell: Auspex would tell the Malk he's being watched, Obfuscate would reverse the rolls, Dominate would be used to interogate an isolated victim for all the information known and then cause an episode of postal. If the malk learns the scale of the operation and gain further leads, they can track down and systematically dismantle everything/hand over the relevant information to kindred authorities for some boon. Given the V5 nerfs to all three of these disciplines, that's somewhat more difficult, but this could happen in every city. The hunters would be killed off before they've made their move, and the rabbit hole can be traveled as far as it goes. Hunters worked because they were disconnected. They shouldn't work better because they all started holding hands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T13:47:21-07:00","id":1386475,"title":"","content":"There are 336,978 people in the US Navy. And of that, 2450 are active duty Navy Seals. 1% of that would be 25 (rounding up) tough mother fuckers, who know how to use strategy, tactics, tools and weapons to win a fight.<br /> <br /> It would probably be easy to find 25 US Navy seals that would jump at a chance to kill vampires. These are the same people who fight terrorists, pirates, and drug cartels all while under difficult conditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T13:51:58-07:00","id":1386479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like CTPhipps list and discussion. This point is also important, and on a related note an area where Fall of London dropped the ball in terms of game design.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like Operation: Antigen in THE FALL OF LONDON is both a representation of both the best and worst elements of the Second Inquisition. The Blade-level technology was particularly notable as was the big epic assaults on Elysium. On the other hand, I think they did a good job setting it up with the fact its made of groups previously familiar to us as well as a indicating they burned all their political capital achieving the cleansing.<br /> <br /> The fact they CAN assault Mithras at the end and get slaughtered down to the last man (if you side with him, he'll exterminate the entirety of the city's hunters) also shows why they DON'T do this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ideally, the SI should serve a similar role in V5 as did the Sabbat in V1 - a menace lurking at the edges of vampire society. A reminder that Camarilla vampires are not the sole predators and masters of the night. The fire, as compared to the frying pan that is normal vampire society (i.e. &quot;out of the frying pan, into the fire&quot;). The dog the steps of every smug and incautious vampire, and they cannot be defeated with some video game style grand standing bullshit... which is why some gamers hate them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that they should be something that Kindred are more paranoid about than actually encountered.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1386475#post1386475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are 336,978 people in the US Navy. And of that, 2450 are active duty Navy Seals. 1% of that would be 25 (rounding up) tough mother fuckers, who know how to use strategy, tactics, tools and weapons to win a fight.<br /> <br /> It would probably be easy to find 25 US Navy seals that would jump at a chance to kill vampires. These are the same people who fight terrorists, pirates, and drug cartels all while under difficult conditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention that there are a very large number of post-active Special Forces types of people who work in PMCs, security, and are just aching for a new job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-07-2020, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T14:00:02-07:00","id":1386480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1386472#post1386472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Electronics hum.</div> </div> </div> </div>An electronics hum? In a city where everything from the art gallery to the garden tool shed is wired for lights? Where the art gallery (and bank, and restaurants, and so on) will also be set up for WiFi, security cameras, televisions, microwaves in the break room and so forth. In a city where 4 out of 5 people are carrying kind of digital device, be it a smartphone, an iPad, or a laptop. In that city and situation a hunter will be found out because they use of electric gizmo? Really? How long would it take to search every single person in even a somewhat crowed room to find who had the actual spy hard ware, and killing everyone in the room would likely be a masquerade violation. And also take a lot of time, before and after.<br /> <br /> It is possible the vampires start meetings and working and scheming in places with no electronic devices or power at all. But nothing presupposes that in your posts or in the setting in general. As a basic thing, a ghoul could be wearing a wire and that would be very hard to detect. And that assumes the hunters are bothering with people on the scene, as compared to remote surveillance, data mining and similar methods.<br /> <br /> And as for the hunters becoming less effective when the (somewhat) work together, you do not seem to understand how logistics works. Which is a bit funny, given your above posting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 05-07-2020, 05:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T14:05:34-07:00","id":1386482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1386472#post1386472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Electronics hum. Not sure if premonition would pick up on it, but heightened senses would. Most elysiums are quiet, controlled places where you'd notice that kinda addition. It'd also make it near joke-easy to find an SI agent tailing a vampire to find out where the vampire goes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that the top of the line bugs would make less noise than the surroundings of a city. Also, that a bug in a cellphone would be, by nature, no more sound than a cellphone makes naturally. Yes, if there's a completely soundless location and they use Auspex they might find it. The Second Inquisition is not invincible. Indeed, I thought my write-up was about how the SI has to be careful and circumspect because it's not invincible.<br /> <br /> You seem to be taking it as a defense of the organization. I think because you don't think there's any way they could do anything against the undead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not that I don't think organized hunter groups should exist, I just know that the scale of the SI is ridiculous. Vampire hunter organizations need to keep themselves secret from other organizations. Because not only are they ideologically different, they're often ideologically incompatible, and on a purely practical level: If you're well connected and one group is compromised, you're all comprimised. </div> </div> </div>Which is part of why they will lose this fight. It's also why they've killed hundreds of vampires so far.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In VTM, a single malk with intent could use the wonderful three disciplines to utterly devastate a cell: Auspex would tell the Malk he's being watched, Obfuscate would reverse the rolls, Dominate would be used to interogate an isolated victim for all the information known and then cause an episode of postal. </div> </div> </div>Yep, if an SI cell is found then they're fucked.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the malk learns the scale of the operation and gain further leads, they can track down and systematically dismantle everything/hand over the relevant information to kindred authorities for some boon. Given the V5 nerfs to all three of these disciplines, that's somewhat more difficult, but this could happen in every city. The hunters would be killed off before they've made their move, and the rabbit hole can be traveled as far as it goes. Hunters worked because they were disconnected. They shouldn't work better because they all started holding hands. </div> </div> </div>Yep. This is a good campaign for PCs to do if they want. You've also described how a SI cell could destroy an entire city's worth of Kindred.<br /> <br /> For the majority of Kindred, they have no interest in fighting the SI. They will immediately sell out their own kind to it, attempt to use it, or protect themselves. The majority of Kindred are not PCs and thus uninterested in engaging with an opponent like the SI. If the Camarilla were united or willing to expend the resources necessary to fight them with heroic self-sacrificing soldiers ready to die to save the vampire race then the SI would be destroyed within a few months.<br /> <br /> Thankfully, for the SI, they aren't and don't. Maybe a few Archons and some ghouls. You work with what you have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-07-2020, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T14:07:38-07:00","id":1386483,"title":"","content":"SI is both too powerful and too weak as presented and that is the really the big problem with them. Schrodinger's Clinton* if will.<br /> <br /> Society of Leopold (or other religious zealots) is going to refuse to &quot;Swat team&quot; a haven? I mean sure they might be smart about do recon and cleanse the whole city at once, maybe poison your herd, bureaucratically get your haven knocked down/excavated during the day, etc , but the devout won't just let you be to go on being an evil affront to God.<br /> <br /> Do you know obvious a drone strike is IRL and the number of people that you'd need on board to even attempt a cover up? They took down the 2nd most supernaturally fortified vampire fortress in the world and cleansed London. They should be able to cleanse the (populated) world of vampires in less than a decade with that level of resources/technology and religious commitment. <br /> <br /> *Schrodinger's Clinton is the theory that the Clintons can kill anyone anytime, no matter how well protected, and get away with it but somehow couldn't use this power to rig an election.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25664-gubenyochi","name":"Gubenyochi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T14:20:12-07:00","id":1386486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gubenyochi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1386483#post1386483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">SI is both too powerful and too weak as presented and that is the really the big problem with them. Schrodinger's Clinton* if will.</div> </div> </div> </div>My list is designed around trying to make a consistent presentation. What did you think?<br /> <br /> But yes, the conflict between the various groups is a definite weakness that will prevent the SI from actually destroying the vampire race. As presented in Chicago by Night, they haven't seen to have impacted the social structure of the city THAT much.<br /> <br /> To use your example:<br /> <br /> <b>Schrodinger's Inquisition</b><br /> <br /> I think the real trick to the Second Inquisition is that it needs to be something that is threatening to the vampire world but not something that is going to utterly destroy the game world. Vampires still must be able to gather at Elysium to have their Eyes Wide Shut orgies. They have to gather at the Succubus Club in order to seduce pretty young things and drink their blood. They need to have sects and clan structures as well as meetings. These are the basis of the game and it's not going to be a gameworld where vampires live solitary lives and pretend to be human 24-7 rather than when only when they're in mixed or Kine company.<br /> <br /> The Second Inquisition does need to be threatening enough that the vampire race is afraid of them, that powerful vampires can be destroyed at seeming random, and they don't know when they are going to strike. To use a possibly tasteless example, the Second Inquisition should be the coronavirus. It's a new threat made from a pre-existing threat that has caused many diverse and disparate reactions among the Kindred race as well as killed a lot of people. There's much disagreement on how to handle it. It will be beaten and the world may (or may not) go back to normal because of it.<br /> <br /> So managing that balance between &quot;this is deadly and dangerous and we need to pay attention&quot; versus &quot;doomsaying&quot; is important. Player characters should be able to fight and kill SI agents, they should be able to evade them, they should be able to potentially hit and wipe out a SI base if they are doing the climax of a Chronicle. They might also get their hacker friend to create a worm that will wipe out all of their information in a cell. They are antagonists that are actually able to be fought and killed unlike Divis Mal or the Archwizards of Shade from Forgotten Realms.<br /> <br /> But they should be strong enough that the players aren't going, &quot;Why doesn't Elminster just kill them?&quot; Except replace Elminster with the Justicars.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T15:59:20-07:00","id":1386520,"title":"","content":"Just throwing out my two cents as someone who likes both V20 and V5 as they are and that fans of both are valid as both has plenty of interesting things to offer, though I lean towards V20 for my personal tastes.<br /> <br /> That disclaimer aside, I for one like CTPhipps list here and thing that it's a really interesting article. I personally wouldn't use V5's Second Inquisition as written for most of my chronicles but a lot of the ideas are interesting and I happily mine them for world building and adding my own personal twist. For most chronicles, except perhaps those focused on vampiric-hunter conflict, I wouldn't formally use the Second Inquisition.<br /> <br /> That said many of the ideas of SI, particularly alongside the setting work we received from Hunters Hunted II is interesting. People have been complaining about (human) hunters lack of bite for years, if not decades, and you can't deny that the Second Inquisition has bite to spare.<br /> <br /> For me, I use something of a middle ground between V20 and V5 as my go-to with adjustment as necessary. There are numerous human hunter organizations (some I take inspiration from HtV for) with the Society of Leopold, SAD, and Arcanum simply being some of the most prominent. These groups largely operate independently and for their own reason and are probably outnumbered by oft-short lived free radicals, hunters without an overarching organization.<br /> <br /> Project Twilight exists within the United States government with many similar organizations worldwide. The Arcanum and other scientist and occultist collectives study the supernatural. The Society of Leopold and other religious organizations still carry the torch against the darkest night spawn. Sometimes rumors arise that loose alliances have formed between members of these organizations with chilling results, yet details remain scant.<br /> <br /> Vampire and hunter society both have legends, rumors, and folklore. Some stories with more validity then others. The urban legend of a ruthless black ops inquisition is a good story for drug-dazed neinates fresh from the rack to share in hushed voices while coming down. Even if most of these stories are nonsense, it only takes one to make a credible threat...<br /> <br /> Like many, if not most things, it comes down to personal taste. Not a particularly satisfying answer I know but one that I honestly think serves as the best possible given most people here and our experience with online debates and how futile they can seem.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm not trying to stifle argument, I think it's interesting to spectate and fun to participate in. So, anyway, that's my two bits, thanks for reading this far y'all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T16:33:50-07:00","id":1386540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1386520#post1386520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just throwing out my two cents as someone who likes both V20 and V5 as they are and that fans of both are valid as both has plenty of interesting things to offer, though I lean towards V20 for my personal tastes.<br /> <br /> That disclaimer aside, I for one like CTPhipps list here and thing that it's a really interesting article. I personally wouldn't use V5's Second Inquisition as written for most of my chronicles but a lot of the ideas are interesting and I happily mine them for world building and adding my own personal twist. For most chronicles, except perhaps those focused on vampiric-hunter conflict, I wouldn't formally use the Second Inquisition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, at the end of the day there's canon but there's also what's true at your table and that's going to be the ST's interpretation of canon. None of it is wrong as the ST is always right. I still play Dungeons and Dragons 3rd Edition instead of trying to update to 5th. Also, I still know people who play 1st Edition Dungeons and Dragons because they are old school with a dash of old school,.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said many of the ideas of SI, particularly alongside the setting work we received from Hunters Hunted II is interesting. People have been complaining about (human) hunters lack of bite for years, if not decades, and you can't deny that the Second Inquisition has bite to spare. </div> </div> </div>I actually felt Hunters Hunted II was a little harsh on the NSA, SAD, and other organizations. They all looked like they took a hit from where they were in 2nd Edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For me, I use something of a middle ground between V20 and V5 as my go-to with adjustment as necessary. There are numerous human hunter organizations (some I take inspiration from HtV for) with the Society of Leopold, SAD, and Arcanum simply being some of the most prominent. These groups largely operate independently and for their own reason and are probably outnumbered by oft-short lived free radicals, hunters without an overarching organization. </div> </div> </div>Do you incorporate H:TR into your world? I tend to have a somewhat iffy view about using them and kind of have them as something that happened in 2000 but fizzled out by 2020. There's only a few left in the world in my WOD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Project Twilight exists within the United States government with many similar organizations worldwide. The Arcanum and other scientist and occultist collectives study the supernatural. The Society of Leopold and other religious organizations still carry the torch against the darkest night spawn. Sometimes rumors arise that loose alliances have formed between members of these organizations with chilling results, yet details remain scant. </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a very solid plan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like many, if not most things, it comes down to personal taste. Not a particularly satisfying answer I know but one that I honestly think serves as the best possible given most people here and our experience with online debates and how futile they can seem.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm not trying to stifle argument, I think it's interesting to spectate and fun to participate in. So, anyway, that's my two bits, thanks for reading this far y'all. </div> </div> </div>Thanks for sharing.<br /> <br /> FYI - I'm debating doing a Ten Tips for the Sabbat in V5 next.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T17:03:27-07:00","id":1386555,"title":"","content":"Some thoughts about how to potentially incorporate the Second Inquisition into a greater World of Darkness. All of this is non-canon of course.<br /> <br /> <b>CT Phipps ideas on the SI and other groups</b><br /> <br /> <b>The Garou and the Second Inquisition</b>: The Garou, for the most part, are unaware of the Second Inquisition and wouldn't care if they were. Their short-sightedness doesn't apply to their Kinfolk, though, who have often been saddled with the thankless job of protecting the Veil. There are dozens of Kinfolk operating within the Second Inquisition and doing their best to prevent the discovery of the Garou's existence. This is a lost cause with the pre-existing hunters like the Society of Leopold, SAD, and Arcanum but many Kinfolk play the role of Scully-esque skeptics who try to paint reports of werewolves as just more Blankbodies (ignoring that they have infrared signatures). The existence of the Gangrel helps them but this is a flimsy protection as is. These Kinfolk are, by and large, supportive of the SI's efforts, though. While the Garou race would be safer if the SI was shut down, many of them actually feel like they're getting to fight the Wyrm for the first time.<br /> <br /> <b>Pentex and the Second Inquisition</b>: Pentex is maintaining a neutral position on the Second Inquisition despite the fact that they have attacked their allies in the Sabbat to a ridiculous degree. Pentex could probably destroy the SI's government support with a few phone calls and maybe eradicate the entire organization if it turned its mammoth resources against it. It doesn't, however, because Pentex doesn't care. While the Sabbat has suffered thousands of losses to Hunters, the destruction of Camarilla elders means that the corporation has gained massive new areas of business to expand their influence into. Pentex has almost no fear for itself and few &quot;valuable&quot; vampire executives while a few less players on the gameboard only benefits it. Were the Masquerade to fall, the corporation would also be first in line to profit from the resulting chaos.<br /> <br /> <b>Hunters and the Second Inquisition</b>: The Imbued are individuals that have been consulted by the Second Inquisition whenever they've been found. Many of these are in prisons or insane asylums after their actions got them captured by mundane authorities. The Second Inquisition is cautious about these people because of their overt supernatural powers as well as general instability. A few have been freed and serve as either full-time consultants or agents on the field. For the larger Imbued organization, they have noticed an uptick in vampire deaths but have yet to be contacted. If they were, they might end up just another arm being fed weapons and equipment or be deemed too much of a security threat.<br /> <br /> <b>The Technocracy and Second Inquisition</b>: The Second Inquisition is something the Technocracy has infiltrated but does not have the time or resources right now to deal with effectively. Operation: Ragnarok resulted in many Technocrats becoming more interested in the threat of vampires but not enough to change policy post-Avatar Storm and dealing with things like Threat Null. As such, the Technocracy serves as an &quot;angel investor&quot; in the Second Inquisition. The perfect storm of funding, support from governments, magically disappearing handicaps to their efforts, and suspicious universality in the decision NOT to go public among its leadership are all the result of the Union helping them from behind the scenes. The Technocracy has also used the SI as a test bed for many low-level devices that would not otherwise work but the Hunters are incredulous enough to operate.<br /> <br /> Despite this, the Technocracy is not actually a fan of the SI. While the die-hard anti-vampire Technocrats (called &quot;The Helsings&quot;) are happy to support it, the organization as a whole considers the group to be a threat to the Timetable. Destroying vampires is something they don't want to leave to amateurs and the disruption of undead society risks exposing the undead to the Consensus. It doesn't help that the SI is allied with religious terrorists like the Society of Leopold and Hermetic affiliated groups like the Arcanum. As such there's a rising number of Unionists who think the SI should be made to go away, regardless of how many reality deviants they've killed.<br /> <br /> The opposition to the SI would grow dramatically if it was known that in addition to the funding and covert support that they've been giving, the Helsings have actually broken protocol and actively launched Ascension War-style raids on powerful vampires. Men in Black, Victors, HIT Marks, and Non-Enlightened soldiers have done a dozen or more missions that they've passed off as the SI. Basically, if a vampire is attacked by what seems like an army and disposable soldiers are used in action movie or comic book fashion then it is almost certainly NOT the SI. The Union can always grow more after all.<br /> <br /> <b>The Traditions and the Second Inquisition</b>: Surprisingly, the SI is ALSO receiving aid from the Traditions or at least two of them. The Celestial Choir and Order of Hermes have been assisting the SI covertly on the religious and occultist end of things without any real contact to the Technocratic assisted end. The Celestial Choir has had agents infiltrated into the Society of Leopold and Catholic Church for years. As such, its Acolytes have found themselves assisting the SI wherever possible with information or freakish strokes of good luck (if not the occasional outright miracle). A few Knights Templar and Celestial Choir paladins have also taken part in hunts. The Order of Hermes has never forgotten its two wars with the Tremere and while perhaps only a dozen Heremetics have been helping the organization, that's enough. Its influence may not be as powerful as the Union but it can pull strings with politicians, corporations, the media and also make sure that attempts to shut down the SI are flummoxed. The Tremere, in particular, doesn't know WHY the Inquisition is almost impossible to track down with magic. The Banu Haqim laughed...and has failed as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-07-2020, 08:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T17:09:33-07:00","id":1386557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1386540#post1386540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you incorporate H:TR into your world? I tend to have a somewhat iffy view about using them and kind of have them as something that happened in 2000 but fizzled out by 2020. There's only a few left in the world in my WOD.</div> </div> </div> </div>I use them as more interesting manifestations of True Faith. Once you accept Blood Magic, Vampires, Ghosts and Lupines are real, a Society of Leopold militant whose True Faith manifests as the gifts of an Avenger instead of the generic \u201chold them back with a crucifix\u201d and similar is just another night in the World of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T17:20:50-07:00","id":1386564,"title":"","content":"Replying to some of the questions and such posed in post #21:<br /> <br /> \u2022Organizations Hit<br /> -I do agree that many hunter organizations were knocked around, particularly in revised and 20th edition story developments and I get what they were going for, I'm just not a fan of it. I keep the government agencies as shadowy but relatively robust although they do have legitimate struggles to avoid getting pressed by mainstream intelligence.<br /> <br /> \u2022The Imbued Question <br /> -I for one, in what may be a somewhat unpopular opinion, like the Imbued and do use them. I've got a reason for them and their history in my own head canon but for the time being I'll say that I do use the Imbued (sometimes called 'Slayers' by other hunters and vampires) as urban legends and rumors of the supernatural world. You're more likely to hear about one then ever see one and you might not realize they actually exist until the white-blood cells of humanity knock down your doors with the wrath of Theseus. <br /> <br /> I also like the points you've made with #22 about how the Second Inquisition might act with other significant supernatural institutions and the image of coming across Imbued in places like prisons and mental asylums does sound interesting to me, particularly how some imbued do become rather radical in their... ehem, 'operating procedures'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T02:43:01-07:00","id":1386655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1386520#post1386520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just throwing out my two cents as someone who likes both V20 and V5 as they are and that fans of both are valid as both has plenty of interesting things to offer, though I lean towards V20 for my personal tastes.<br /> <br /> That disclaimer aside, I for one like CTPhipps list here and thing that it's a really interesting article. I personally wouldn't use V5's Second Inquisition as written for most of my chronicles but a lot of the ideas are interesting and I happily mine them for world building and adding my own personal twist. For most chronicles, except perhaps those focused on vampiric-hunter conflict, I wouldn't formally use the Second Inquisition.<br /> <br /> That said many of the ideas of SI, particularly alongside the setting work we received from Hunters Hunted II is interesting. People have been complaining about (human) hunters lack of bite for years, if not decades, and you can't deny that the Second Inquisition has bite to spare.<br /> <br /> For me, I use something of a middle ground between V20 and V5 as my go-to with adjustment as necessary. There are numerous human hunter organizations (some I take inspiration from HtV for) with the Society of Leopold, SAD, and Arcanum simply being some of the most prominent. These groups largely operate independently and for their own reason and are probably outnumbered by oft-short lived free radicals, hunters without an overarching organization.<br /> <br /> Project Twilight exists within the United States government with many similar organizations worldwide. The Arcanum and other scientist and occultist collectives study the supernatural. The Society of Leopold and other religious organizations still carry the torch against the darkest night spawn. Sometimes rumors arise that loose alliances have formed between members of these organizations with chilling results, yet details remain scant.<br /> <br /> Vampire and hunter society both have legends, rumors, and folklore. Some stories with more validity then others. The urban legend of a ruthless black ops inquisition is a good story for drug-dazed neinates fresh from the rack to share in hushed voices while coming down. Even if most of these stories are nonsense, it only takes one to make a credible threat...<br /> <br /> Like many, if not most things, it comes down to personal taste. Not a particularly satisfying answer I know but one that I honestly think serves as the best possible given most people here and our experience with online debates and how futile they can seem.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm not trying to stifle argument, I think it's interesting to spectate and fun to participate in. So, anyway, that's my two bits, thanks for reading this far y'all.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's more-or-less how I'd use it. No way I'd use them as written, but a downplayed version, like this, I think is an interesting addition and yes, a logical outgrown of the earlier material in prior editions and Hunters Hunted 2 a lot more than what got into V5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T08:20:09-07:00","id":1386697,"title":"","content":"Given that the only people who like vampires are people they have enslaved with the blood bond or dominate, I suspect any of the splats that learn about the SI will think it is a good idea, to some degree. So, from the Mage side I can see some Ether types working on and off with a local SI chapter to work on weapons, vehicles and tools. Likewise for the VA, who would help with tracking, data mining, and burning down someone's credit rating and financial accounts. The Euthanitos and Verbena would be happy to return the blood suckers to the cycle of life. And so on. These contributions would be small scale compared to that of other SI partners, but meaningful to the vampires who just found their haven repossessed and crawling (during the day) with people using light-based weapons which should not work but do anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T00:47:46-07:00","id":1386926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1386697#post1386697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that the only people who like vampires are people they have enslaved with the blood bond or dominate, I suspect any of the splats that learn about the SI will think it is a good idea, to some degree. So, from the Mage side I can see some Ether types working on and off with a local SI chapter to work on weapons, vehicles and tools. Likewise for the VA, who would help with tracking, data mining, and burning down someone's credit rating and financial accounts. The Euthanitos and Verbena would be happy to return the blood suckers to the cycle of life. And so on. These contributions would be small scale compared to that of other SI partners, but meaningful to the vampires who just found their haven repossessed and crawling (during the day) with people using light-based weapons which should not work but do anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not true. The nebulous group known as &quot;vampires&quot; have big, generous wallets and have been a significant aid to people in power; They've lobied extensively, financed campaigns, kept the right people in power and they've added growth and propserity to a lot of organizations. Many vampires have great personal charisma and magnetism, and many have offered delights widely considered off-limits. Sure, they may have knocked down some losers, but those people lost, and thus have no real power. Vampires are absolute delights in our neoliberal world. The vampires are friends with the heads of police departments, mayors, governors, the political parties (not just the winning one) big business, Unions, loby groups and think tanks, televangelists and television. Vampires don't control all of this because of 'disciplines' indeed, the Ventrue disdain the use of disciplines for this kind of thing, they just go in with a winning smile and a bag filled with all the things someone might want. Money, sex, drugs, a new house, help with that lawsuit... Vampires make friends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T00:50:27-07:00","id":1386927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1386926#post1386926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is not true. The nebulous group known as &quot;vampires&quot; have big, generous wallets and have been a significant aid to people in power; They've lobied extensively, financed campaigns, kept the right people in power and they've added growth and propserity to a lot of organizations. Many vampires have great personal charisma and magnetism, and many have offered delights widely considered off-limits. Sure, they may have knocked down some losers, but those people lost, and thus have no real power. Vampires are absolute delights in our neoliberal world. The vampires are friends with the heads of police departments, mayors, governors, the political parties (not just the winning one) big business, Unions, loby groups and think tanks, televangelists and television. Vampires don't control all of this because of 'disciplines' indeed, the Ventrue disdain the use of disciplines for this kind of thing, they just go in with a winning smile and a bag filled with all the things someone might want. Money, sex, drugs, a new house, help with that lawsuit... Vampires make friends.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have a weird idea anyone in the world of darkness likes vampires. They're the Malfoys. Lots of people bow to the fear and money they have but no one LIKES the Malfoys.<br /> <br /> Not even other Deatheaters.<br /> <br /> Or to put it into another perspective, vampires are just another international crime syndicate like the mafia or the cartels. They wield enormous power over governments, finance, and local communities but no one LIKES organized crime.<br /> <br /> Indeed, that's why the Masquerade exists because if all of humanity knew about the undead then they'd destroy them because humans don't even like each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T04:24:55-07:00","id":1386946,"title":"","content":"I feel like you've just put a lot less thought into it than i have.<br /> Brujah, Toreador, Ventrue. The first two are everywhere; They're by far the most common vampire types. the later two are generally the leaders of vampire society when it comes to dealing with mortals. These guys all have Presence as an in-clan discipline, and to support presence you need a lot of charisma; these clans have a lot of personal charm and magnetism because they typically embrace from people with charm and magnetism. Hanging around people with a lot of charisma is generally indicative of a good time, and you don't have to be a settite to give the people what they want. The Malkavians, Nosferatu and Gangrel have next to no presence among mortals (well, two of them might, but they also have obfuscate) and the Lasombra/Giovanni (Two agressive people-clans that aren't so good to hang out with, if we just look at the paper) aren't really that common. And the Tremere... they'll embrace one person with charm to make up for the other six that'll stay inside and read all day. <br /> <br /> Vampires have plenty of mundane charm. Pre-V5, you weren't going to have a good time using social disciplines if you didn't have great mundane social powers in the first place, and whilst borish players who insist on getting away with the worst behaviours because they've got 4/5 in their socials are a thing (and plenty of players have been won over by that guy with supposedly 1 charisma) that's generally not the case with NPCs. If the average Ventrue has 4 ettiquete, why wouldn't he be an absolute delight to talk to when he wants to talk to you? And if you're a politician with peculiar and abhorrent sexual interests and someone offers you a risk-free line that you can continually benefit from so long as policy occasionaly goes her way, what would it matter that she has some very pale skin and you only see her during the evening? What exactly makes vampires worse friends than any other person of importance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T09:02:05-07:00","id":1386984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1386946#post1386946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like you've just put a lot less thought into it than i have.<br /> Brujah, Toreador, Ventrue. The first two are everywhere; They're by far the most common vampire types. the later two are generally the leaders of vampire society when it comes to dealing with mortals. These guys all have Presence as an in-clan discipline, and to support presence you need a lot of charisma; these clans have a lot of personal charm and magnetism because they typically embrace from people with charm and magnetism. Hanging around people with a lot of charisma is generally indicative of a good time, and you don't have to be a settite to give the people what they want. The Malkavians, Nosferatu and Gangrel have next to no presence among mortals (well, two of them might, but they also have obfuscate) and the Lasombra/Giovanni (Two agressive people-clans that aren't so good to hang out with, if we just look at the paper) aren't really that common. And the Tremere... they'll embrace one person with charm to make up for the other six that'll stay inside and read all day.<br /> <br /> Vampires have plenty of mundane charm. Pre-V5, you weren't going to have a good time using social disciplines if you didn't have great mundane social powers in the first place, and whilst borish players who insist on getting away with the worst behaviours because they've got 4/5 in their socials are a thing (and plenty of players have been won over by that guy with supposedly 1 charisma) that's generally not the case with NPCs. If the average Ventrue has 4 ettiquete, why wouldn't he be an absolute delight to talk to when he wants to talk to you? And if you're a politician with peculiar and abhorrent sexual interests and someone offers you a risk-free line that you can continually benefit from so long as policy occasionaly goes her way, what would it matter that she has some very pale skin and you only see her during the evening? What exactly makes vampires worse friends than any other person of importance?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because, they may have supernatural charisma. They may have money. They might offer temptations of forbidden delight. But even in previous editions, Vampires have the masquerade for a reason. Because. Even if vampire society has every politician kissing their boots. It doesn't matter.<br /> <br /> Vampires are the other. They are the literal parasites of the 1%, they regularly commit murders, they regularly brainwash people, they frequently commit all sorts of abuse. Outside of the religious concerns (Which you aren't going to win over. We've seen exactly how well that went. There was this thing called the Inquisition) there is the common man who suddenly has a very easy target to lash out at. Vampires, people who literally have to be blood sucking monster's to live, people who are at risk of blowing up and going on a murder spree in the middle of a crowd because someone called them a name.<br /> <br /> To use the U.S. as an example, we certain sections of the country were good friends with the germans and it was taught fairly commonly as a language. Then the world wars happened and the common person turned against them. No real concern for the muslim population, and then for the most recent and noted example, 9/11 happened. The common man wasn't too fond of people of the muslim religion or anyone associated with the middle east in general.<br /> <br /> A cynic might say that's because they had resources, but vampires have tons of resources and an easy way of negating their legality to get those resources to other people. But the thing is.outside of dictatorships, leaders have to at least pretend to be acting in the best interest of their population whether that be a moral or tangible benefit. Vampires as a species really don't get to claim that as they are. Again. Parasites. They aren't symbiotes. They aren't benevolent leaders. They might win over a crowd temporarily, but there are hunters who would be happy to kill even a 'legal' vampire. Especially when said vampire ate their relative/friend/coworker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T11:32:23-07:00","id":1387023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1386927#post1386927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have a weird idea anyone in the world of darkness likes vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>To put it another way, vampires are what happens if terminal cancer could put on nice clothing and have dance parties and run your company. Normal people would, at best tolerate this because it was the social order and it provides a (meager) paycheck. Others might exploit it. But one one, who was not the vampire/cancer, would <i>like it</i>.<br /> <br /> Aside from that, in terms of money and wealth... what is to keep another group of splats (mages, werewolves, etc) from going full D&amp;D on the vampires; i.e. why not kill the vampire and loot the lair for everything they can load into a truck? Nothing helps inter Tradition (or Tribe) bonding quite like an old fashioned monster hunt and then stealing all the monster's stuff.<br /> <br /> Vampires are monsters. That is the point of the game - deal with being a monster while living a secret life. They are not put upon fashionable types with solar urticaria (sun allergy). Vampires are, by definition, bad people. Bad people acquire enemies because they are bad people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 05-09-2020, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T12:13:08-07:00","id":1387036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1386486#post1386486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My list is designed around trying to make a consistent presentation. What did you think?<br /> <br /> But yes, the conflict between the various groups is a definite weakness that will prevent the SI from actually destroying the vampire race. As presented in Chicago by Night, they haven't seen to have impacted the social structure of the city THAT much.<br /> <br /> To use your example:<br /> <br /> <b>Schrodinger's Inquisition</b><br /> <br /> I think the real trick to the Second Inquisition is that it needs to be something that is threatening to the vampire world but not something that is going to utterly destroy the game world. Vampires still must be able to gather at Elysium to have their Eyes Wide Shut orgies. They have to gather at the Succubus Club in order to seduce pretty young things and drink their blood. They need to have sects and clan structures as well as meetings. These are the basis of the game and it's not going to be a gameworld where vampires live solitary lives and pretend to be human 24-7 rather than when only when they're in mixed or Kine company.<br /> <br /> The Second Inquisition does need to be threatening enough that the vampire race is afraid of them, that powerful vampires can be destroyed at seeming random, and they don't know when they are going to strike. To use a possibly tasteless example, the Second Inquisition should be the coronavirus. It's a new threat made from a pre-existing threat that has caused many diverse and disparate reactions among the Kindred race as well as killed a lot of people. There's much disagreement on how to handle it. It will be beaten and the world may (or may not) go back to normal because of it.<br /> <br /> So managing that balance between &quot;this is deadly and dangerous and we need to pay attention&quot; versus &quot;doomsaying&quot; is important. Player characters should be able to fight and kill SI agents, they should be able to evade them, they should be able to potentially hit and wipe out a SI base if they are doing the climax of a Chronicle. They might also get their hacker friend to create a worm that will wipe out all of their information in a cell. They are antagonists that are actually able to be fought and killed unlike Divis Mal or the Archwizards of Shade from Forgotten Realms.<br /> <br /> But they should be strong enough that the players aren't going, &quot;Why doesn't Elminster just kill them?&quot; Except replace Elminster with the Justicars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a fan of your list, but your explanation here is exactly how they SHOULD have been presented and would have made the situation much more believable to me. Killing a few random named NPCs to show that they are scary but strike with precision and careful planning. Unfortunately the whole world setting now relies on them basically killing Elminster in his most defensible position as their introduction. This sets their base power level. Combining that with &quot;Blankbody&quot; detectors, it's only a matter of time that they wipe the civilized world clean. A few dual camera spy satellites shouldn't be a problem for people who can disguise a drone strike (which is about as subtle as crashing a plane into a building).<br /> <br /> It will always come down, for me, to what would it take game MECHANICS wise Pre-V5 to accomplish taking down the Tremere chantry? And that is the power level the SI has to be at to be believable and at that level they might as well be antediluvians as far as PCs are concerned. Personally I need my fluff supported by the mechanics for an RPG to be enjoyable, your preferences may differ.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25664-gubenyochi","name":"Gubenyochi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T12:36:32-07:00","id":1387044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gubenyochi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1387036#post1387036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not a fan of your list, but your explanation here is exactly how they SHOULD have been presented and would have made the situation much more believable to me. Killing a few random named NPCs to show that they are scary but strike with precision and careful planning. Unfortunately the whole world setting now relies on them basically killing Elminster in his most defensible position as their introduction. This sets their base power level. Combining that with &quot;Blankbody&quot; detectors, it's only a matter of time that they wipe the civilized world clean. A few dual camera spy satellites shouldn't be a problem for people who can disguise a drone strike (which is about as subtle as crashing a plane into a building).</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I think they're limited by the fact:<br /> <br /> 1. Thermal optics don't work on the Blush of Life<br /> 2. There's not that many of them overall.<br /> 3. They're keeping themselves and their goals secret<br /> 4. They're eventually going to run out of money if they haven't already<br /> 5. They're not that united.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It will always come down, for me, to what would it take game MECHANICS wise Pre-V5 to accomplish taking down the Tremere chantry? And that is the power level the SI has to be at to be believable and at that level they might as well be antediluvians as far as PCs are concerned. Personally I need my fluff supported by the mechanics for an RPG to be enjoyable, your preferences may differ. </div> </div> </div>Frankly, I think the Tremere Chantry was destroyed purely to get rid of the Transylvania Chronicles leftover plot of the Antediluvian Worm Thing. It had grown completely out of control and into a confusing mess. Also, some weird retcons had been made like, &quot;It can't be seen by mortals and teleports daily.&quot; Which seems more M:TA than V:TM. It was probably an inside job but I think that getting rid of the plot was a good idea overall.<br /> <br /> Were I to rewrite it, I'd say that Tremere/Goratrix took down the wards and they dropped the bomb on the place because it was Tremere's will that the Worm Thing be buried under a ton of rubble. It was his influence and power that made sure the SI got away with it on Austrian soil and that everyone bought their cover story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T14:01:55-07:00","id":1387073,"title":"","content":"Vampires are less &quot;The other&quot; and more &quot;caricatures of real people&quot;. They're parasites that feed on literal blood, they can make friends with parasites who feed on the metaphorical blood of the working man. Exploiting people is how the 0.01% work, a vampire doing it more literally isn't going to be all that off putting for them. Especially in the world of darkness, the elites are corrupt; White collar crime is the norm, not the exception, and many knowingly collude with pedaphiles, never mind your average rapist. What's a vampire to such a person? Racism is for the poor, when you're rich, it's about controling the poor and keeping your buddies above scrutiny less that scrutiny turn to you. Morality will make you poor. Vampires make excellent friends to elites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T22:01:41-07:00","id":1387176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1387073#post1387073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires are less &amp;quot;The other&amp;quot; and more &amp;quot;caricatures of real people&amp;quot;. They're parasites that feed on literal blood, they can make friends with parasites who feed on the metaphorical blood of the working man. Exploiting people is how the 0.01% work, a vampire doing it more literally isn't going to be all that off putting for them. Especially in the world of darkness, the elites are corrupt; White collar crime is the norm, not the exception, and many knowingly collude with pedaphiles, never mind your average rapist. What's a vampire to such a person? Racism is for the poor, when you're rich, it's about controling the poor and keeping your buddies above scrutiny less that scrutiny turn to you. Morality will make you poor. Vampires make excellent friends to elites.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, some folks on this thread act like someone finding out their biggest donor is a vampire would mean instant retribution. People in the real world regularly take money from and rub shoulders at parties with humans that do far worse than drink blood and it doesn't seem to bother them one bit as long as it's kept behind closed doors.....or semi-ajar doors at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T22:07:42-07:00","id":1387178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1387176#post1387176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, some folks on this thread act like someone finding out their biggest donor is a vampire would mean instant retribution. People in the real world regularly take money from and rub shoulders at parties with humans that do far worse than drink blood and it doesn't seem to bother them one bit as long as it's kept behind closed doors.....or semi-ajar doors at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>We also have people who are being shot for arbitrary aspects of gender, race, and other reasons. I think being walking corpses and drinking blood would result in a far far bigger reaction.<br /> <br /> Mind you, in my games when the Second Inquisition hit places, they tend to mysteriously miss the super-rich.<br /> <br /> It's just most vampires aren't the super-rich.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T22:21:39-07:00","id":1387182,"title":"","content":"Not sure why the non-sequiter about how fucked the US is culturally...but ok.<br /> <br /> Of course we're discussing rich vamps aka the Cam Ventrue etc. when we're talking about political donations and power. I'm just saying that the people who regularly take kickbacks and donations from human traffickers, pederasts, rapists, slavers, torturers etc. are not even going to blink if they got a peek behind the mask, and those that would make damn sure they never look.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T22:26:57-07:00","id":1387184,"title":"","content":"I'd wager a much larger percentage of the vampire population are in the top ten percentile than a similar sized human population would be. Simply through accumulation if nothing else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T22:46:19-07:00","id":1387191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1387182#post1387182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure why the non-sequiter about how fucked the US is culturally...but ok.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you mean. It's a statement that human beings will react to the Other with violence, especially one like vampires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course we're discussing rich vamps aka the Cam Ventrue etc. when we're talking about political donations and power. I'm just saying that the people who regularly take kickbacks and donations from human traffickers, pederasts, rapists, slavers, torturers etc. are not even going to blink if they got a peek behind the mask, and those that would make damn sure they never look. </div> </div> </div>Yes, hence why I mentioned it as &quot;11#: They're not the good guys.&quot; Mind you, said people will still hunt and exterminate vampires to benefit themselves.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T14:52:21-07:00","id":1387333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1387191#post1387191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure what you mean. It's a statement that human beings will react to the Other with violence, especially one like vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>People shooting unarmed people because of the colour of their skin is about Power, if you think its about Fear of the Other your buying into the line the guy holding the gun wants you to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T14:53:43-07:00","id":1387334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1387333#post1387333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> People shooting unarmed people because of the colour of their skin is about Power, if you think its about Fear of the Other your buying into the line the guy holding the gun wants you to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fear of losing one's privileges over an oppressed and abused minority is just a different way of saying the same thing.<br /> <br /> I used Fantastic Racism (See TVtropes.org) as an element in my United States of Monsters books and contrasted is to actual racism against minorities as a plot point. Peter Stone, the star of STRAIGHT OUTTA FANGTON, is a black man as well as a vampire while so is his creator. The character gets to discuss the fact that there's plenty of hate toward both but with vastly different reasons as well as what sort of differences that it means for a person who is both. The Maven of the Eventide discusses the issues brought up in her review of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/_1tQwK2PnOA\" data-code=\"_1tQwK2PnOA\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/_1tQwK2PnOA/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> For me, hatred as a motivation of the Second Inquisition is an interesting way of depicting their motivations as they are less about the actual damage that vampires do or threats than a blind and unthinking revulsion at the idea of people who are fundamentally different than them. The existence of vampires challenges the status quo where the governments as well as majorities who make them up believe themselves to be the top of the world.<br /> <br /> There's a lot that can be done with the fact the vampire race challenges notions of superiority and dominance in their culture that is reasonably post-racial, post-sexism, and pansexual (hemosexual?). For a thoroughly unpleasant SI, you can have the decision to destroy the undead motivated by someone who fears that they upend the social order, especially when confronted by the fact vampires can wield substantial authority as minorities.<br /> <br /> Or it can all just be because they're bloodsucking corpses. Depends on how you want to process the themes of your campaign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-10-2020, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T12:42:40-07:00","id":1389420,"title":"","content":"I've developed a soft spot for Dark Ages Inquisitor so I've been toying with this idea that the Second Inquisition is a bit like a modernized version of that (the 'Shadow Inquisition') It might have its roots in different groups (Society of Leopold, Project Twilight, etc.) banding together along with the Imbued (probably the soldiers) who may have gotten an upgrade (Inquisitor in many ways feels like what upgraded Hunters might be like) and alot of the human factions touched by (and fighting) against the supernatural have some sorts of common threads that could tie them together (Hunter: First Contact and Time of Judgement even alluded to such possibilities. Hunter:Utopia may have been another idea for that.)<br /> <br /> Even if they are a more organized amalgam of diffrerent Human factions you would still probably see a ton of nuance (and problems arising from differences in philosophy, belief, etc.) Like the most visible face of the 2nd Inquisition has been explicitly militant and intolerant but like the Society of Leopold and Hunters before it there can be lots of factionalism under the surface and different attitudes towards their supernatural 'adversaries' and their influence in the larger organization can wax and wane as circumstances evolve. Ultimately I treat it as more of a centralized doorway to having humanity play in the realm of the supernatural (which is a bit more like Hunter the Vigil I suppose.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25533,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","user":"Mister_Dunpeal","date":". 05-17-2020, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T14:13:11-07:00","id":1389750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition#post1386135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>8. The Second Inquisition isn't listening to your phone (probably)</b><br /> <br /> The Second Inquisition isn't using PRISM to monitor the entire internet for any mention of Camarilla, Anarchs, Brujah, or Beckett. Even if they could, they wouldn't be able to sort through all of the data or justify it to other government branches. The Kindred don't understand their enemy or its capabilities, so that's partially why the SI continues to bedevil them. They can hack the computers and phones of those Kindred they identify but it's usually a much more personal as well as slow-going process. The paranoia about one vampire potentially exposing many others is not entirely unjustified, though. How screwed are you if they have a bug in Elysium? The Succubus Club? Or more? Perhaps very or perhaps not at all as everyone uses an alias. It's all up to the Storyteller. It's also possible that the guy monitoring those places will stick his findings in a pile of papers that will never be read or be an agent of another power.</div> </div> </div> </div>So your suggestion for running the SI is to nerf their one actual competitive advantage into the ground?<br /> <br /> Carry a cellphone? Well you better be tossing it in the trash on a daily basis because that phones location data is being stored 24/7 and whenever a vamp is detected or captured, one of the first things done is to grab everything from their phone and get to work building out the contact map.<br /> <br /> Where has this cellphone been? What other phones have been in the same locations at the same times? What numbers does the phone call, what numbers do those phones call?<br /> <br /> All of the &quot;possibles&quot; are tagged, tapped, and traced. Every call and text from everyone of them is being reviewed in realtime.<br /> <br /> Link a car to a vamp? Well then traffic cam footage is pulled to start backtracing its location and every bit of paperwork related to it gets put under the microscope.<br /> <br /> The SI is a threat precisely because they are able to turn the full might of the NSA, CIA, Treasury, IRS, FBI, MI6, MI5, FSB, Mossad, and MSS against vamps in a coordinated manner and the vampires are absolutely <i>not </i>up to date on how to avoid modern surveillance capabilities.<br /> <br /> So yes, when the SI goes hot and starts moving against vampires they already have most vamps IDed, localized, and being tracked in real time. They know who the active power brokers are, where everyone shelters, where Elysium is, what corporate and governmental resources are under vamp control, etc.<br /> <br /> If you want to avoid the SI then what a vamp should do is immediately toss <i>everything</i> and go off grid as they rebuild from the ground up. At the same time they should be throwing lots of problems at the SI. The global economy is crashed, the Lasombra detonate a Russian nuke in the ME to sink a US carrier, scandal after political scandal hits the web &amp; papers as centuries of dirty laundry is brought out and made public, local police are dominated into bad shoots, bioweapons are released, etc. The vamps throw the world into so much chaos and disorder that the structures of the mortal world and the infrastructure that the SI is reliant on ceases to function.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25361-sagacious-gamer","name":"Sagacious Gamer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T23:09:50-07:00","id":1389870,"title":"","content":"A suspected vampire who's being tailed by the SI can almost certainly count on having their phone permanently switched on and transmitting to a recorder. That's at least one order of magnitude in difference from scouring the entirety of global communications and trying to filter literally all the data in the world to look for vampires. It's just a matter of how much work load can feasibly be tackled. In the real world, the NSA had to outsource their illegal domestic surveillance work to private contractors in order to manage it all, and that was with a threat that everyone believed existed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T03:53:10-07:00","id":1389921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1389870#post1389870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A suspected vampire who's being tailed by the SI can almost certainly count on having their phone permanently switched on and transmitting to a recorder. That's at least one order of magnitude in difference from scouring the entirety of global communications and trying to filter literally all the data in the world to look for vampires. It's just a matter of how much work load can feasibly be tackled. In the real world, the NSA had to outsource their illegal domestic surveillance work to private contractors in order to manage it all, and that was with a threat that everyone believed existed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> When I wrote that my take on the subject was not, &quot;The Second Inquisition CAN'T listen to your phone&quot;, my subject was, &quot;The Second Inquisition has 7 billion people to listen to and probably isn't because there's too much data to sort through. When you're caught, that's a different story.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T07:16:45-07:00","id":1389962,"title":"","content":"I think, amid all the Watsonian quibbling the topic of the SI encourages, its useful to analyze the Doylist reasons for its existence and its role in the setting:<br /> <br /> 1) It\u2019s meant to emphasize the importance of the Masquerade, especially after the game had drifted away from that understanding because of power creep etc., to where mortals seemed like chumps and vampires untouchable. Instead of retconning that stuff away, V5 basically says yes, vampire authorities get cocky and overreached, and now there\u2019s blowback. Because underestimating mortals was vampires\u2019 original error that led to the creation of the Camarilla etc., and it was time for a reminder.<br /> <br /> 2) It\u2019s meant to reflect how this sort of thing might look in a post 9/11 world, wherein major states have assumed a broad mandate to combat terrorism, they often cooperate and outsource those efforts, their operatives have extraordinary powers and little accountability, and large scale surveillance of civilian populations is now considered normal. It just doesn\u2019t make sense that all of these things could have progressed in this way, yet none of it would have any consequences for vampires. In a way, the SI is necessary to make the setting feel like it\u2019s progressed out of the 90s.<br /> <br /> 3) It also emphasizes the cyclic nature of the setting, which is a big thing in V5 in particular. Vampires have been here before but failed to learn from it and keep making the same mistakes because they\u2019re selfish and short-sighted. It\u2019s what the Noddist myths try to warn the Kindred about. Now things have played out in a way eerily reminiscent of first inquisition, with vampires trying to use mortal hunters against each other, panicked elders throwing their childer under the bus to save themselves, a general doubling down on secrecy, and these badass creatures of the night being reminded that, in the end, vampires <i>parasitize</i> human civilization \u2014 they don\u2019t <i>run</i> it.<br /> <br /> With those things in mind, it\u2019s just a matter of taste how an individual storyteller uses the SI, and there doesn\u2019t even need to be any uniformity. But as a concept it does make sense, and moreover it heartens back to the early days of Vampire when hunters were meant to be frightening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":352,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","user":"Black Flag","date":". 05-19-2020, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T12:33:30-07:00","id":1390028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1389870#post1389870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A suspected vampire who's being tailed by the SI can almost certainly count on having their phone permanently switched on and transmitting to a recorder. That's at least one order of magnitude in difference from scouring the entirety of global communications and trying to filter literally all the data in the world to look for vampires. It's just a matter of how much work load can feasibly be tackled. In the real world, the NSA had to outsource their illegal domestic surveillance work to private contractors in order to manage it all, and that was with a threat that everyone believed existed.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1389921#post1389921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes.<br /> <br /> When I wrote that my take on the subject was not, &quot;The Second Inquisition CAN'T listen to your phone&quot;, my subject was, &quot;The Second Inquisition has 7 billion people to listen to and probably isn't because there's too much data to sort through. When you're caught, that's a different story.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The NSA doesn't really outsource its surveillance work, it outsources to get the tools but not generally for the use of said tools.<br /> <br /> And no, it's not that hard to filter the data. The phone companies know every phone call that your phone has ever made, have records of every text you've ever sent, and know your phones location down to at least the city block at essentially all times; and the SI has (or could easily get) access to that data.<br /> <br /> It all just sits there in the database until a phone linked to a vampire (or other target) is identified. Once that happens that phones history is correlated with the database as a whole; who did it call or text, what websites did it visit, how long were its calls, when were those calls made, etc. And most importantly, what other phones were in the same locations at the same time.<br /> <br /> With one phone you go from seven billion people to track down to a relative handful. You start building up a contact map and mapping out the social circle, overlaying it with the circles of other vampires. In very short order you have an incredibly complete map of the entire network.<br /> <br /> You also look at financial records for all of those phones. Who are they legally registered to, who is paying the bills, how are those bills being paid, what is the billing address for the phone (and associated bank accounts)? What other things are associated with those accounts or addresses?<br /> <br /> Let's say that the vamps are using VPN's and highly encrypted channels to communicate. That protects the <i>content</i> of the communication but it also makes it stand out like a light in a dark room. The worlds traffic is filtered first for anything using that particular encryption scheme and then further filtered to identify the nodes of the VPN network. Once the nodes are IDed, a tag is simply added to all traffic exiting those nodes and traced to the end users. Again, identifying the phones/computers used by the vamps isn't beyond their reach and once done those devices are tracked in real time.<br /> <br /> Hiding from the NSA alone is so hard as to be essentially impossible. The vamps, at least the elders and sects, have the resources to actually be able to do so to some extent though. Hiding from the NSA when they are working in coordination with the FSB, MSS, etc. becomes nigh totally impossible. You simply can't actually ghost your way through the telecommunications system against that kind of opposition.<br /> <br /> Even flat out owning the telecom companies (which the Cam probably does via the Venture) only works until that control is established; and then it just becomes all the easier to identify the network.<br /> <br /> Can an individual or a small group beat the system? Absolutely, if they have resources, knowledge, skills, and don't make mistakes. Can an organization the size of the Cam or Sabbat, and with their needs to be at least semi-public do it? Not a chance. There will always be a breach and once the first opening is found, the resources that the likes of the NSA can bring to bare as a <i>casual</i> matter will bring down the entire network.<br /> <br /> As for concealing this all from their bosses? Vampires get marked as a terrorist organization or two, are given a code name, and the entire compartment is buried as TS/SCI; and probably ghosted onto another TS/SCI project to cover some of the resource use. All that shows up in the records (assuming that you are one of the handful of people who could ever see said records in the first place) is a log entry in the database with a project codeword as authorization and access beyond that point requires that the individual trying to access it be cleared for that compartment already.<br /> <br /> For the intel work, more money doesn't need to be appropriated nor does new equipment need to be built. It really is as easy as some coding and the authority to bury one more routine task into the already extant infrastructure.<br /> <br /> You have something like the Society of Leopold acting as a clearing house for the data, probably with their own infiltrators or recruits actually in those intel agencies handling that end. And the Society was probably damn careful to make sure that everyone with the ability to identify their intel sources has True Faith so that they can't be mind fucked into turning traitor. They synthesize the intel into a mission order and whatever facts (shorn of any hint of sources or methods) are needed to complete that mission and then pass it on to a strike team. Any captured team member knows nothing beyond their own cell; they have their own training facilities, own armories, own communications networks, own bank accounts, own cash, etc. and orders/intel is received via dead drop (which might literally be a drone dropping a package on their back porch at two in the morning while they sleep).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1389962#post1389962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think, amid all the Watsonian quibbling the topic of the SI encourages, its useful to analyze the Doylist reasons for its existence and its role in the setting:<br /> <br /> 1) It\u2019s meant to emphasize the importance of the Masquerade, especially after the game had drifted away from that understanding because of power creep etc., to where mortals seemed like chumps and vampires untouchable. Instead of retconning that stuff away, V5 basically says yes, vampire authorities get cocky and overreached, and now there\u2019s blowback. Because underestimating mortals was vampires\u2019 original error that led to the creation of the Camarilla etc., and it was time for a reminder.<br /> <br /> \u200b2) It\u2019s meant to reflect how this sort of thing might look in a post 9/11 world, wherein major states have assumed a broad mandate to combat terrorism, they often cooperate and outsource those efforts, their operatives have extraordinary powers and little accountability, and large scale surveillance of civilian populations is now considered normal. It just doesn\u2019t make sense that all of these things could have progressed in this way, yet none of it would have any consequences for vampires. In a way, the SI is necessary to make the setting feel like it\u2019s progressed out of the 90s.<br /> <br /> 3) It also emphasizes the cyclic nature of the setting, which is a big thing in V5 in particular. Vampires have been here before but failed to learn from it and keep making the same mistakes because they\u2019re selfish and short-sighted. It\u2019s what the Noddist myths try to warn the Kindred about. Now things have played out in a way eerily reminiscent of first inquisition, with vampires trying to use mortal hunters against each other, panicked elders throwing their childer under the bus to save themselves, a general doubling down on secrecy, and these badass creatures of the night being reminded that, in the end, vampires <i>parasitize</i> human civilization \u2014 they don\u2019t <i>run</i> it.<br /> <br /> With those things in mind, it\u2019s just a matter of taste how an individual storyteller uses the SI, and there doesn\u2019t even need to be any uniformity. But as a concept it does make sense, and moreover it heartens back to the early days of Vampire when hunters were meant to be frightening.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Except, being honest, mortals are still chumps and vampires are still largely untouchable. The SI works much better as a catspaw for some number of proper elders/meths who have decided that the world needs to be reordered; there are too many neonates being made, vampire society needs to be reformed to keep up with the drastic changes in technology over the past century, and its a time for a bit of proper revenge.<br /> <br /> A bare handful of BH, Ventrue, and Nos Elders/Meths could have done it pretty easily. Once Ur-Shulgi awoke, the Tremeres nights were numbered; there was <i>no</i> way that he was going to let that cursing stand and so plans are modified.<br /> <br /> The Nos Elder ensures that the existence of ShreckNet leaks to the other Clans and that the Nos concede to the demands of the Ventrue (pressed by their own Elder(s)) to allow the other clans access. Said access is provided, except the ShreckNet that outsiders are allowed to access is nothing but a decoy; oh the information is real and it appears complete but a great many secrets were kept off this network. ShreckNet (the fake) gets purposefully leaked to the right mortals via the Ventrue and their pawns in the mortal governments. And when they are ready, the SI goes active. The BH with Ur-Shulgi at its head defang the Tremere and destroy their Chantry; and walk right into an alliance with the Ventrue without any issue. The mortals, obviously, prioritize the Sabbat as they are both easier to find and more <i>monster</i> but a great deal of the Camarillia riff-raff also finds the mortals breaking down their doors as Meths have no real use for most Princes who still count their unlives in a handful of centuries; if the vamps have any worth then they will survive the mortals anyways. The Lasombra leadership is right there on board with this plan, purging their own ranks and the Sabbat of many of the &quot;problem&quot; individuals while sliding into the new alliance.<br /> <br /> The Beckoning? The Ghennah War? It's amazing the lies that a handful of 4th and 5th Generation Meths working together can pull off. All those meths suddenly awaken and all the elders are moving to the ME for this war; what rich hunting grounds. What a great way to get the ignorant neonates and newblood (only a few centuries, why they are still practically babes) without sense to rush to a prepared killing ground - a killing ground on the doorstep of the clan of Assassins and where the mortals are very apt to look the other way and think nothing of chaos. But what about those who return high on power and with tales of the War? You think a Meth can't pull off pretending to be a young vamp who diableried a Meth?<br /> <br /> As for the Second Inquisition; the Cam still has all that middle management that needs to be cleared out, distracted, and played for fools. So the Ventrue string pullers pass down orders to cause chaos for the mortals. Dangerous viruses are unleashed, the markets and corporate books are played with the cause issues, etc. China and the EU are both sitting on economic bombs that could bring down their economies at any point and they have been in place for years; the Ventrue should have zero problem causing that collapse. What happens to China when its bubble bursts and the government can no longer feed itself? What happens when Iran and Saudi Arabia throw a war and imperil global energy supplies (which a vamp could engineer with trivial ease)? What happens when the Euro collapses and takes with it the entire idea of European unity? What happens in the US when the political process is turned farcical and social unrest is being pushed, when the cartels become more violent, etc.? What happens when the Pope is assassinated and replaced with a hardline conservative diametrically opposed to the policies of the previous Pope?<br /> <br /> All that nice shiny chaos to distract the mortals and let the SI tear itself apart after it has done its work; as the resources the SI depends on to be any kind of threat cease to be available. And then, after the SI's purpose has been served, the Meths get together and do a little housecleaning of their own to cut it back down to size as just another group of hunters.<br /> <br /> The only way that the V5 metaplot actually makes any sense in relation to the previous VtM lore &amp; history is if the entire plot is basically Meths playing games for their own purposes. The mortals think they are doing something, the young vamps are all proud of themselves for throwing off their Elders and gaining power &amp; prestige, the arrogant Elders are running around like chickens with their heads cut off as they got complacent; and behind it all the Meths remain, just as secure as they have always been and still playing their own games with a world that they control and have controlled for, quite literally, thousands of years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25361-sagacious-gamer","name":"Sagacious Gamer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T12:40:33-07:00","id":1390031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sagacious Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1390028#post1390028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The NSA doesn't really outsource its surveillance work, it outsources to get the tools but not generally for the use of said tools.<br /> <br /> And no, it's not that hard to filter the data. The phone companies know every phone call that your phone has ever made, have records of every text you've ever sent, and know your phones location down to at least the city block at essentially all times; and the SI has (or could easily get) access to that data.<br /> <br /> It all just sits there in the database until a phone linked to a vampire (or other target) is identified. Once that happens that phones history is correlated with the database as a whole; who did it call or text, what websites did it visit, how long were its calls, when were those calls made, etc. And most importantly, what other phones were in the same locations at the same time.<br /> <br /> With one phone you go from seven billion people to track down to a relative handful. You start building up a contact map and mapping out the social circle, overlaying it with the circles of other vampires. In very short order you have an incredibly complete map of the entire network.<br /> <br /> You also look at financial records for all of those phones. Who are they legally registered to, who is paying the bills, how are those bills being paid, what is the billing address for the phone (and associated bank accounts)? What other things are associated with those accounts or addresses?<br /> <br /> Let's say that the vamps are using VPN's and highly encrypted channels to communicate. That protects the <i>content</i> of the communication but it also makes it stand out like a light in a dark room. The worlds traffic is filtered first for anything using that particular encryption scheme and then further filtered to identify the nodes of the VPN network. Once the nodes are IDed, a tag is simply added to all traffic exiting those nodes and traced to the end users. Again, identifying the phones/computers used by the vamps isn't beyond their reach and once done those devices are tracked in real time.<br /> <br /> Hiding from the NSA alone is so hard as to be essentially impossible. The vamps, at least the elders and sects, have the resources to actually be able to do so to some extent though. Hiding from the NSA when they are working in coordination with the FSB, MSS, etc. becomes nigh totally impossible. You simply can't actually ghost your way through the telecommunications system against that kind of opposition.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd THINK that.<br /> <br /> My thoughts on the subject are influenced by the Netflix episode of DIRTY MONEY called &quot;Cartel Bank&quot; where the National Security Agency had the full suspicions that a international bank was laundering money. One of the fascinating things was the insight into their monitoring the banks, phone calls, e-mails, and so on. The incompetence on display, failures, and easy evasions were fascinating to watch as was the fact their top priority was thirty nerds on computers bored out of their minds. This for a supposedly high priority international terrorism and arms trafficking ring.<br /> <br /> One fascinating moment was where one of the employees cracked the code (i.e. the cartel leaders were adding a 1 to every one of their transactions names so they didn't show up in the search engine) and couldn't get his employers to change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T12:49:17-07:00","id":1390036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1390031#post1390031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You'd THINK that.<br /> <br /> My thoughts on the subject are influenced by the Netflix episode of DIRTY MONEY called &quot;Cartel Bank&quot; where the National Security Agency had the full suspicions that a international bank was laundering money. One of the fascinating things was the insight into their monitoring the banks, phone calls, e-mails, and so on. The incompetence on display, failures, and easy evasions were fascinating to watch as was the fact their top priority was thirty nerds on computers bored out of their minds. This for a supposedly high priority international terrorism and arms trafficking ring.<br /> <br /> One fascinating moment was where one of the employees cracked the code (i.e. the cartel leaders were adding a 1 to every one of their transactions names so they didn't show up in the search engine) and couldn't get his employers to change.</div> </div> </div> </div>The NSA doesn't do criminal cases. HSBC was being looked at by the FBI and Treasury on tips from a lot of sources (including the NSA) but what, if anything, the NSA knew about them and when is still classified TS/SCI and will remain that way for at least the next forty or so years. Given that the CIA was running money through them for covert operations; the US national security establishment was fully aware of the money laundering going on.<br /> <br /> Criminal cases have been tossed before because the NSA flatly told the judge that they would not be sharing evidence with the Court; they really do not care about criminality or criminal prosecution (and being honest, any attempt to charge someone on the basis of NSA provided intel is going to end up tossed by the courts). Where the NSA matters is if you are important enough to the US for the CIA to want you dead or if you are a foreign nation state.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25361-sagacious-gamer","name":"Sagacious Gamer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T12:53:42-07:00","id":1390038,"title":"","content":"I stand corrected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T13:49:35-07:00","id":1390053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sagacious Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1390028#post1390028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The only way that the V5 metaplot actually makes any sense in relation to the previous VtM lore &amp; history is if the entire plot is basically Meths playing games for their own purposes. The mortals think they are doing something, the young vamps are all proud of themselves for throwing off their Elders and gaining power &amp; prestige, the arrogant Elders are running around like chickens with their heads cut off as they got complacent; and behind it all the Meths remain, just as secure as they have always been and still playing their own games with a world that they control and have controlled for, quite literally, thousands of years.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... was the first inquisition also a sham? Is the Masquerade unnecessary because of how all mortals are impotent? Is the only way to square things with the lore to... imagine that all the lore is false?<br /> <br /> Even if I could understand all of that, the really important question is, does it make for a better game? I can't see how that would be the case. I mean, it's not called Vampire: the No Fucks Given Because We're Untouchable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T15:30:44-07:00","id":1390078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1390053#post1390053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... was the first inquisition also a sham? Is the Masquerade unnecessary because of how all mortals are impotent? Is the only way to square things with the lore to... imagine that all the lore is false?<br /> <br /> Even if I could understand all of that, the really important question is, does it make for a better game? I can't see how that would be the case. I mean, it's not called Vampire: the No Fucks Given Because We're Untouchable.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You mean the First Inquisition that was started by vamps to kill other vamps and advance vamp goals until it got out of hand in conjunction with the vamp civil war that was going on at the time?<br /> <br /> The First Inquisition that didn't appear to actually do much of anything when it comes to killing powerful vampires or reducing their ability to influence the mortal world.<br /> <br /> This also being the same First Inquisition that was operating in a world that was much harder for vampires to hide in?<br /> <br /> The Masquerade is necessary for reasons that have little to nothing to do with the potency (or lack thereof) of the regular mortals. If Vampires rule openly then you establish an immortal aristocracy that is easily definable to the masses as <i>other</i> and that is pretty much anathema to the beliefs of those masses. Because new vampires are always going to be made, you can't play into the otherness as a means of establishing divine right. If you allow mortals to rule alongside the vampires then those mortals will, almost inevitably, end up vamp patsies or turned themselves. Why all this matters is that the kine become a great weapon for vamps that want to improve their position to grab. A vamp helps the mortals end the current vamp ruler in the hope of taking the rulers place; and until you get to the real top tier vamps, a large number of mortals is still a real threat.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, mortals can be encouraged to fear vampires and think them fiction &amp; myth. The powers that be among the Kindred can still do what they will with the mortals with little to no fear or interference in their business; but those mortals cease to be a viable weapon to be used against them. The hungry neonate simply won't be able to raise a mortal force large enough to be a serious threat to a proper Elder - especially not while keeping his plans secret. The younger vampires are at risk from relatively small groups of Hunters and their own predilections ensure that most mortals will be unwilling to work with those younger vampires. More importantly, the Masquerade and fear of the mortals gives the Elders a ready made excuse to end younger vampires; framing someone for a Masquerade breach is so very easy after all. It is also a great way to gain favors and control those younger vampires; they need identities, properties, bank accounts, etc. They need mortal authorities to look the other way; and who controls all of those levers of mortal society that the neonate needs if he wants to avoid breaching the Masquerade? Why the Elders of course.<br /> <br /> The Masquerade is about control, but it is about controlling the younger vampires.<br /> <br /> As for ruling the mortals? They still do, it's just that instead of being the King ruling from a castle they are the reclusive family with a large stock portfolio. Open rulership invites challenge, blame, and responsibility. Instead of, for example, being the Judge it is much easier to own the Judge by keeping his daughters cancer at bay. Instead of Dominating the Senator, you simply donate some money and use Auspex to get prime blackmail material.<br /> <br /> It's a lighter touch but is all the more powerful, insidious, and inescapable for precisely that reason. Convince the mortals that you don't exist, divide their lines of authority to ensure dispersed (and redundant) control, and pull the strings while the mortals are secure in the knowledge that they control their own fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25361-sagacious-gamer","name":"Sagacious Gamer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T15:35:51-07:00","id":1390081,"title":"","content":"Ah, I've got it. You're an Anarch infiltrator. Welcome, comrade! When is the revolution?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T15:36:15-07:00","id":1390082,"title":"","content":"My simple response is, &quot;Thematically, Hunters being under control of vampires is uninteresting as a campaign element to explore. Humans should be more than just pawns.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T15:42:53-07:00","id":1390083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1390082#post1390082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My simple response is, &quot;Thematically, Hunters being under control of vampires is uninteresting as a campaign element to explore. Humans should be more than just pawns.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, though there are some people to whom it's apparently very important that vampires rule and mortals drool. V3 did seem to promote that view, by implicaton if not explicitly, in contrast to pretty much every other edition. But as the last one before the hiatus, it's been very influential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T16:27:47-07:00","id":1390089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1390082#post1390082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My simple response is, &quot;Thematically, Hunters being under control of vampires is uninteresting as a campaign element to explore. Humans should be more than just pawns.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? Does it matter to the neonate (the vast majority of PC's) who is ultimately behind the Hunters? As far as the neonate is concerned, its some mortals hunting them; and to get to the vamp pulling the strings usually requires several iterations of unknowing patsies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1390083#post1390083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed, though there are some people to whom it's apparently very important that vampires rule and mortals drool. V3 did seem to promote that view, by implicaton if not explicitly, in contrast to pretty much every other edition. But as the last one before the hiatus, it's been very influential.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mortals are inherently disadvantaged against vampires in ways that can't be overcome. Vampires are <i>immortal</i>. They don't die of old age and, for the ones that last at least, think nothing of plans that take decades (or longer) to come to fruition.<br /> <br /> Start with the lowest level neonate in, say, the modern US. Who are they going to hunt? The average wage slave or the street corner drug dealer? An upstanding citizen goes missing and you get police investigations, missing persons posters, angry family, etc. The average gang-banger goes missing? No one really cares. Now what does said average gang-banger have on them? Cash and objects easily convertible to cash. With a little thought, said neonate realizes that Dominating or blood bonding that banger is all it takes to start rolling up the gang and locating their stash house.<br /> <br /> A vampire with nothing but the clothes on their back stepping into any city on the planet should have a few hundred thousand in cash inside a week or two. Seed capital is simply <i>easy</i> for vampires.<br /> <br /> Crime is <i>easy</i> when you can use supernatural powers to ensure the loyalty of your underlings. Once the money is laundered and the right paperwork drawn up, the vampire becomes just one more millionaire with a hefty stock portfolio watched over by a money manager at a major bank. And then comes the fun of compounded interest and investment returns when you have minimal living expenses and immortality. This is without getting into things like insider trading, stock manipulation, theft, etc.<br /> <br /> That wealth, and its attendant influence, builds year after year, decade after decade, century after century. And that is before you have an entire clan specifically focused on gaining wealth and using it to influence mortal institutions. Any Ventrue Elder worth the name will be controlling <i>billions</i> in assets; the clan as a whole will literally have a degree of wealth that makes the House of Saud look like paupers.<br /> <br /> Politicians get bought, civil servants get influenced, media is controlled, etc. In other words, all of the organs that mortal humanity uses to organize itself and control its combined efforts are co-opted by vampires with ease.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> Let's think easy examples. You're a vampire and you want to build influence. Now you could go and thrall a school Principal, for example. But he interacts with the government and other mortals of influence, he is also a potential mark for other vampires and may well show up at the same place as other vampires. It is also notable if he goes nuts. Or you can quietly influence the schools janitor one night to gain access to the building; where you install a keylogger on the Principals computer to capture his info, put a few hidden cameras in the ladies bathrooms to gather some CP to frame him with in the future, etc. With access to the student records you have their names, addresses, parents info, etc. In addition to getting a leg up on the competition via seeing who is liable to be useful in future (and a lot of PII to steal and use for your own benefit), you also gain a bit of potential influence. And when you want that Principal to do something? Well a phone call and some instructions and he is looking at a few gigs of CP of his students sitting on his school issue computer in a hidden file; he can play ball or a routine audit of the schools computer network is going to find the CP and his life is ruined. And those claims of innocence? Well those will be doubted when he commits suicide one day. Or, instead, he can do whatever it is you want.<br /> <br /> You can turn the police officer, or instead you can turn the police department's mechanic and a small tweak gives you real time tracking data on the entire police fleet along with access to their radio network. Need to run a plate? Well the trojan sitting in the in-car laptop of one of those officers will take care of that without anyone the wiser.<br /> <br /> You want the DA on your side? Well that is high profile. But turning his cleaning service to plug a USB drive into his home computer? Much easier, and it spreads when he connects his cellphone. After that it is simply a matter of finding out what leverage you need to encourage the result you want.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> Playing mortals and influencing their society to one's own benefit is <i>easy</i> for any vampire; much less an organized group of vampires that have been active since, literally, before the US was a nation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25361-sagacious-gamer","name":"Sagacious Gamer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T16:31:15-07:00","id":1390091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sagacious Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1390089#post1390089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? Does it matter to the neonate (the vast majority of PC's) who is ultimately behind the Hunters? As far as the neonate is concerned, its some mortals hunting them; and to get to the vamp pulling the strings usually requires several iterations of unknowing patsies.</div> </div> </div> </div>To keep my answers, simple, yes. It's important that humans don't be treated as cattle or unimportant because that dehumanizes them and makes the game solely about vampires versus vampires living in a vampire world.<br /> <br /> It also negates the idea that if the PCs get caught, the vampires are dead. Fear of discovery is a major element in my games and that's why vampires are terrified of even the tiniest breach of the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> In one Chicago by Night 5E chronicle I run, I said that the Second Inqusition had destroyed half of all vampires in the world by 2019.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T16:57:35-07:00","id":1390102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1390091#post1390091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To keep my answers, simple, yes. It's important that humans don't be treated as cattle or unimportant because that dehumanizes them and makes the game solely about vampires versus vampires living in a vampire world.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, you and I see the objectification of humanity as an obvious source of horror in the game. Clearly there are others for whom it's pure power fantasy and a source of enjoyment in itself.<br /> <br /> I mean, people can take their jollies how they like, I guess, but I can't help finding that worldview less than attractive. It's also not very informed by history or, you know, actual human behavior. It's more like conspiracy-theory thinking, where monolithic all-powerful institutions are capable of locking down everything without fail, without flaw. Never mind that's just not how people work, and even vampires don't have enough supernatural mojo to predict and control large numbers of people.<br /> <br /> The assertion that nobody would care if a gang member died is very telling. It's a perspective from which people aren't really <i>people</i>, they're just statistics at best.<br /> <br /> Suffice it to say, as a historian I have to suggest that humans are a lot more chaotic in their behavior than these armchair analyses tend to suggest. However, vampires <i>thinking </i>humans are this easy to control explains a lot of their failures over the centuries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T17:00:55-07:00","id":1390104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1390091#post1390091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To keep my answers, simple, yes. It's important that humans don't be treated as cattle or unimportant because that dehumanizes them and makes the game solely about vampires versus vampires living in a vampire world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Humans <i>are</i> cattle in a vampire game. That is half the angst of the neonate; accepting that their old tribe is now their food supply. Vampires are <i>monsters</i>, even the most cultured of them. Vampires care about humanity the same way that a farmer cares about his sheep; he wants them happy, comfortable, and secure from the wolves while he shaves them bare on a regular basis for his own benefit and seperates out a portion for dinner.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It also negates the idea that if the PCs get caught, the vampires are dead. Fear of discovery is a major element in my games and that's why vampires are terrified of even the tiniest breach of the Masquerade. </div> </div> </div>If the PC's get caught; they are still dead. The Hunters that they are dealing with don't have any clue that they are vamp pawns, those hunters bosses don't even realize that <i>they</i> are vamp pawns. As for the Elders/Meths actually behind the Hunters in the end; what do they care about some uppity neonates clearly too incompetent and worthless to save? Afterall, the PC's got caught by humans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In one Chicago by Night 5E chronicle I run, I said that the Second Inqusition had destroyed half of all vampires in the world by 2019. </div> </div> </div>Only half? Between the SI, the Lasombra betrayal, the BH's revenge, and the Genhanna War; I go with north of 90% of the worlds vampire population dead inside a handful of years.<br /> <br /> What matters though is <i>who</i> is doing the dying. Pretty much every vampire under 200 is dead (or will be dead in relatively short order).<br /> <br /> The SI comes into a city and does the first cleansing pass; and in their wake come the BH kill teams with full records provided by the Nos, Ventrue, and Lasombra to get anyone the SI missed who isn't specifically under the protection of a major power.<br /> <br /> The Lasombra gutted the Sabbats leadership and middle ranks and turned over contingency plans and safehouse locations to the BH. Whose to say what Sabbat packs actually went to the ME and which ones died in their homes unaware they were targets, only for their nominal superior to say that they had &quot;gone off to war&quot; to any who asked?<br /> <br /> Those younglings that manage to survive? Well they were clearly something special and deserving of unlife. The vast majority that end up destroyed? Good riddance, there were too many of them anyways.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs? Well what is more likely, that a 200 year old 9th gen managed to off Hardestadt or that the 900+ year old 6th gen (perhaps lower) who essentially built the Camarilla is playing games and faked his death? Because Bell getting away with that positioned him perfectly as the figure for the younger generations and the Anarchs to rally around. Whether he is a knowing or unknowing agent, he is in a prime position to keep those who can't abide the Camarilla under control and pass on the needed information to purge any troublemakers.<br /> <br /> I mean what actually happened in V5? The Ventrue, Nos, BH, and Lasombra have managed to guy every real competing power base and build an alliance that is set to control Kindred society for centuries to come. The Sabbat are broken and are unlikely to ever recover (the Anarchs are recruiting most of the vamps that would otherwise go Sabbat), the Anarchs are led by a former Archon who is somehow getting a pass for offing his boss and turning traitor in the most public manner possible and his faction has the Brujah, Gangrel, and Followers of Set (much reduced in power thanks to the GW taking place in their home territory) as its dominant players (none of which are noted for being all that good at building organizations or with philisophies that make them anything but allies of neccessity).<br /> <br /> V5 Camarilla is, relative to the other factions, more powerful than it has ever been. And its leadership got to purge unreliable/ill-fitting elements and replace them with ones that are more onboard with its methods and more reliable. All while also gutting all of its real opposition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25361-sagacious-gamer","name":"Sagacious Gamer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T17:03:33-07:00","id":1390105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sagacious Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1390104#post1390104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humans <i>are</i> cattle in a vampire game. That is half the angst of the neonate; accepting that their old tribe is now their food supply. Vampires are <i>monsters</i>, even the most cultured of them. Vampires care about humanity the same way that a farmer cares about his sheep; he wants them happy, comfortable, and secure from the wolves while he shaves them bare on a regular basis for his own benefit and seperates out a portion for dinner.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that would be the attitude of which you're supposed to fight. It's also wrong in-universe because it leads to arrogance like thinking you can manipulate the NSA or the Catholic Church.<br /> <br /> I think our biggest difference here is that both of us feel like the Camarilla views humans like you're describing. But it's correct at your table while it's a sign of just how out of touch and arrogant they are at mine.<br /> <br /> I think it changes the themes of the game a great deal if the Camarilla are right about humans or if they're playing with fire (and pitchforks).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-19-2020, 08:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T17:33:59-07:00","id":1390117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1390105#post1390105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, that would be the attitude of which you're supposed to fight. It's also wrong in-universe because it leads to arrogance like thinking you can manipulate the NSA or the Catholic Church.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who is supposed to fight this attitude? The Storyteller? The universe? The players? The PC's?<br /> <br /> As for thinking you can manipulate the NSA or Catholic Church being arrogance; why? The CC might have some advantages/defenses thanks to its nature and history, but it has been the playground of vamps in the past (The Lasombra most notably).<br /> <br /> But otherwise? They are just human institutions with no inherent defenses against the supernatural or vampire abilities.<br /> <br /> Do you think that the Ventrue would have any real issue getting their chosen candidate elected to the Senate? When they control media companies, have billions of dollars to throw around, are utterly amoral, and think nothing of staging scandals for the opposition? Not to mention Auspex provided Telepathy to literally read the oppositions secrets from their own minds. Once you have your Senators, it is only a matter of time before they can get on the Senate Intelligence Committee. In other words, the body charged with oversight of the NSA.<br /> <br /> Infiltrating your agents is, again, not that hard and only a matter of time. Would a vamp think anything of adopting an orphan, indoctrinating him from early childhood, having him join the military, and getting him in a position to start working at the NSA? Your spy needs someone removed? Well a traceless assassination is easy for a vamp. He needs to look good? Well just feed him some vamp provided intel.<br /> <br /> The Church? The Papacy itself has been bought and sold before, not to mention all of the lesser offices. Again, Auspex is your friend. Anyone with True Faith is easy to detect with that and thus gets to be the victim of a mugging, or have a tragic car accident, or some other lethal experience. Anyone without? Well telepathy and putting their lives under a microscope let you find the ones who are viable targets for control and what approach to use. And once you have your Priest, well it becomes fairly trivial to engineer their promotion to more influential office. More, once you turn a few it becomes trivial to use them to promote your other pawns. And what do you know, a century or two later you have a steady supply of Cardinals and Bishops under your thumb. And all without anything so obvious (or detectable) as a blood bond or Discipline; just normal human corruption, fear, and self interest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think our biggest difference here is that both of us feel like the Camarilla views humans like you're describing. But it's correct at your table while it's a sign of just how out of touch and arrogant they are at mine.<br /> <br /> I think it changes the themes of the game a great deal if the Camarilla are right about humans or if they're playing with fire (and pitchforks). </div> </div> </div>For the Camarilla to be wrong about humans you need to either <i>massively </i>increase the abilities of humans or <i>massively</i> nerf vampires; as in vampires are no longer immortals or vampires can no longer have any hope of passing for (or interacting with) human. Because immortality and sociopathy (which will be a trait that virtually any vampire that lasts has) are enough on their own to control <i>any</i> human institution given enough time. With the rest of their supernatural powers you have to be an incredibly incompetent vampire to fail at establishing that control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25361-sagacious-gamer","name":"Sagacious Gamer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T17:37:05-07:00","id":1390118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sagacious Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1390117#post1390117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Camarilla to be wrong about humans you need to either <i>massively </i>increase the abilities of humans or <i>massively</i> nerf vampires; as in vampires are no longer immortals or vampires can no longer have any hope of passing for (or interacting with) human. Because immortality and sociopathy (which will be a trait that virtually any vampire that lasts has) are enough on their own to control <i>any</i> human institution given enough time. With the rest of their supernatural powers you have to be an incredibly incompetent vampire to fail at establishing that control.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, that gets to the heart of our disagreement. Because I believe the Camarilla is wrong about humans, the Second Inquisition makes perfect sense to me. Because you don't, it's ridiculous.<br /> <br /> In simpler terms, &quot;None of a vampire's magical powers should make up for their weaknesses as well as sheer numbers from humans.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T17:53:21-07:00","id":1390126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1390118#post1390118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Basically, that gets to the heart of our disagreement. Because I believe the Camarilla is wrong about humans, the Second Inquisition makes perfect sense to me. Because you don't, it's ridiculous.<br /> <br /> In simpler terms, &quot;None of a vampire's magical powers should make up for their weaknesses as well as sheer numbers from humans.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Numbers only matter when they have targets, are coordinated, and are acting for a unified purpose.<br /> <br /> Numbers without all of those features just work against one another and get nothing done.<br /> <br /> Vampires are hard to find both individually and as a collective whole; hence finding targets is a non trivial challenge.<br /> Humans are hard to coordinate, this is exactly why governments and corporations exist. Humanity is not a hive mind, but if you control the bodies used to coordinate a group of people then you render those numbers meaningless.<br /> Humans need a unified purpose; without one the group will be working against itself.<br /> <br /> If the drug cartels and terrorist organizations can remain effective and powerful, why do you think that vampires couldn't be at least as effective and powerful?<br /> <br /> You seem to operate on the assumption that all vampires are Edward Cullen or Angel; angsting away their days whining about &quot;poor me&quot; and how the world has shat on them. Newsflash; the vast majority of those whiny little shits die within a few years of being turned. They either can't handle the dissonance between what they need to do to survive and their previous morality or their whining anonys someone with the power to end them and they get to meet the sun.<br /> <br /> For every Edward, Angel, or Louise there are a hundred Aro's, Spike's, or Lestat's. And that is before you get into the fact that Siring is a selective process.<br /> <br /> You think that a Ventrue or Lasombra is ever going to turn an emo whiner who will bemoan the realities of unlife? Fuck no.<br /> <br /> Turning those who won't get with the program is a waste of a precious resource (permission to sire) and makes the Sire look bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25361-sagacious-gamer","name":"Sagacious Gamer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T17:56:50-07:00","id":1390128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sagacious Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386135-ten-tips-for-running-the-second-inquisition?p=1390126#post1390126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Numbers only matter when they have targets, are coordinated, and are acting for a unified purpose.<br /> <br /> Numbers without all of those features just work against one another and get nothing done.<br /> <br /> Vampires are hard to find both individually and as a collective whole; hence finding targets is a non trivial challenge.<br /> Humans are hard to coordinate, this is exactly why governments and corporations exist. Humanity is not a hive mind, but if you control the bodies used to coordinate a group of people then you render those numbers meaningless.<br /> Humans need a unified purpose; without one the group will be working against itself.<br /> <br /> If the drug cartels and terrorist organizations can remain effective and powerful, why do you think that vampires couldn't be at least as effective and powerful?<br /> <br /> You seem to operate on the assumption that all vampires are Edward Cullen or Angel; angsting away their days whining about &quot;poor me&quot; and how the world has shat on them. Newsflash; the vast majority of those whiny little shits die within a few years of being turned. They either can't handle the dissonance between what they need to do to survive and their previous morality or their whining anonys someone with the power to end them and they get to meet the sun.<br /> <br /> For every Edward, Angel, or Louise there are a hundred Aro's, Spike's, or Lestat's. And that is before you get into the fact that Siring is a selective process.<br /> <br /> You think that a Ventrue or Lasombra is ever going to turn an emo whiner who will bemoan the realities of unlife? Fuck no.<br /> <br /> Turning those who won't get with the program is a waste of a precious resource (permission to sire) and makes the Sire look bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the contrary, I believe the vast majority of vampires are vindictive sociopaths. Which makes them LESS able to function in the face of human resistance and MORE likely to screw up.<br /> <br /> Edward Cullen may be a complete joke [his WOD version ends up killing Bella in the woods due to a failed Hunger roll] but he and his clan are actually better prepared to survive the Second Inquisition because living in the middle of bumfuck nowhere, eating animals, and not dropping bodies everywhere is the key to avoiding unnecessary attention from mortals.<br /> <br /> The older a vampire gets, the more arrogant and confidant of their powers they are. Which can really result in them getting fucked because there's just as many human geniuses out there as there are undead. The Elders tend to be more cunning because it takes a lot to survive that long but there's plenty of human Caesars, Draculas, and Pattons.<br /> <br /> One of my favorite moments from VTDA is the statement Dracula captured a 4th generation Vampire and 5th with his armies before torturing the secrets of immortaliy out of them.<br /> <br /> But again, this is a description of taste and themes. Neither of us is wrong in how we do our games. It's just choosing what themes to emphasize.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-20-2020, 08:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T05:10:40-07:00","id":1390257,"title":"","content":"Getting the NSA to deal with Vampires is dumber than stealing a modern main battle tank to take on your local teen hooligans. It's one thing to say &quot;huh, vampires are arrogant&quot; and another to say &quot;Vampires really, really like overkill&quot;. Playing vampire, for me, is all about the fear of doing something wrong and getting caught for it. While I did just write a big thread on why the masquerade's strong, that doesn't mean you should take the piss. You don't want to get something you can't control into your problems, especially when there are far easier paths to take. Career Criminals don't call the police on each-other like children getting the teacher involved. Everybody loses when the Masquerade goes up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T12:17:57-07:00","id":1390357,"title":"","content":"I tend to view both human 'hunters' (including the Second Inquisition) as well as Vampire sects as not operating in isolation. They're both influencing the same system. There are more of humans and (as we saw in Gehenna) if enough of humanity mobilized with a goal of eradicating the Vampire sects.. they could do it.* Problem is, getting humans to unify like that requirs a pretty major motivation most of the time. And the Camarilla (and to an extent the Sabbat) are good at neutralizing those threats by manipulating the system. They have the skills and experience to head it off BEFORE it becomes a problem most of the time.<br /> <br /> But that 'not in isolation' extends beyond the sects and humanity. There are other factions (Werewolves, the Wyrm factions, The Traditions and Technocracy, the Mummies and Changelings, etc. And that isn't including the supernaturals of other countries/continents either.) Those are all factions operating in the same system and that creates a complex interplay of forces and influences that can be hard for any one faction to predict or control with any reliability** and that will impact the success and failure of any given faction's venture. Compound that with the fact that - at times - factions can cooperate intentionally or not. (IIRC for example, the Technocracy has known Vampires prey on humans and have infiltrated human society. But a combination of limited resources and higher priorities means that as long as Vampires don't rock the boat the Technocracy will overlook them. For now. Hell, the Technocracy's desire to maintain the status quo means they're just as apt to help maintain something like a Masquerade because it serves their interests as much as the Camarillas. So its not just the Camarilla sect acting in that respect. Likewise we know that Vampires are usually thought of as wyrm entities, so the Wyrm factions have an interest in supporting/protecting vampires as well. Whether the vampires know it or not. )<br /> <br /> Ultimately you have a situation that maintains a balance where no one side is likely to gain dominance for long until some other factor (Again like the Week of Nightmares, the Sixth Maelstrom or Gehenna/Time of Judgement) is sufficiently 'big' enough to outweigh all other factors. It's alot more dynamic and (to me at least) less boring because there's more potential for uncertainty and conflict and sudden reversals. It denies humanity the chance to bring its mass and power to bear (a conventional conflict where they could eradicate the Vampire sects) but it also limits the Sect's ability (and other factions) totally and persistently dominating humanity the way they did in the First City or as outlined in the Book of Nod.<br /> <br /> Besides, if you pay attention to the larger connected metaplots, any resolution between humanity and the supernatural isn't likely to come from conventional conflict of one side conquering/wiping out the other. It will get resolved in other ways. So the fighting, scheming, and politicking is really just a way to pass the time and hold your own until that point is reached.<br /> <br /> *what happened if the Ancient Vampires awoke is another matter, again as Gehenna showed. Even the Week of Nightmares demonstrates that factions like the Technocracy may have limits (at least within the Vampire setting.)<br /> <br /> **outside the respective setting's super-powered entities. Antediluvians, Mage Oracles, Methuselahs and Archmages, and so on. Indeed I suspect all those factions play a role in maintaining the various secret facades and act covert because acting openly would be the supernatural equivalent of a nuclear war. Magical MAD (Mutually Assured Destruction). Or: Rock Falls, everyone dies. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}